{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9hZLdANfkufWzR427dgVg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Hires Profiling\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B hires bf16 2-bit-only profiling（48 layers × 8 KV heads = 384 heads）。 测试 diagnostic 是否在 Qwen 模型族内泛化。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"qwen14b_baseline_ppl\": 5.84,\n7\t      \"qwen14b_top5_concentration\": 0.55,\n8\t      \"qwen14b_t1_t5\": 0.63,\n9\t      \"qwen14b_l0_dominance_ratio\": 8.2,\n10\t      \"qwen14b_top1_head\": \"L0H2\",\n11\t      \"qwen14b_top1_delta_2bit\": 3.81,\n12\t      \"qwen14b_l0_4heads_total_share\": 0.41,\n13\t      \"qwen14b_delta_2bit_cv\": 5.12,\n14\t      \"qwen14b_positive_delta_heads\": 370,\n15\t      \"qwen14b_total_heads\": 384,\n16\t      \"qwen14b_distribution_shape\": \"borderline_spread\",\n17\t      \"diagnostic_prediction\": \"Spread (conc≥0.50 AND t₁/t₅≤0.70)\",\n18\t      \"diagnostic_correct\": false\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"name\": \"Qwen Family Profiling Comparison\",\n23\t        \"columns\": [\n24\t          \"model\",\n25\t          \"layers\",\n26\t          \"kv_heads\",\n27\t          \"concentration\",\n28\t          \"t1_t5\",\n29\t          \"l0_share\",\n30\t          \"top1_delta\",\n31\t          \"shape\"\n32\t        ],\n33\t        \"rows\": [\n34\t          [\n35\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n36\t            28,\n37\t            112,\n38\t            0.61,\n39\t            0.57,\n40\t            \"58.6%\",\n41\t            6.74,\n42\t            \"Spread\"\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n46\t            48,\n47\t            384,\n48\t            0.55,\n49\t            0.63,\n50\t            \"41.0%\",\n51\t            3.81,\n52\t            \"Diluted Spread\"\n53\t          ]\n54\t        ]\n55\t      }\n56\t    ],\n57\t    \"figures\": [],\n58\t    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic 两个指标都刚过阈值（concentration 0.55 > 0.50, t₁/t₅ 0.63 < 0.70）， 但边际通过。14B 的关键问题：更多层分摊了 sensitivity，使得 L0 的 dominance 不足以 让 MCKP 产生有意义的 allocation 差异。这暴露了 joint diagnostic 的 boundary fragility—— 阈值在 border 附近不 robust。\\n\\n\\nQwen2.5-14B 有 48 layers × 8 KV heads = 384 heads（vs 7B 的 28×4=112）。 GQA 仍是 7:1，保留 L0 某些 heads 的较高 sensitivity（concentration=0.55，刚过 0.50 阈值）。 但 14B 的 L0 cluster 比 7B 弱得多：7B 的 L0 4 heads 占 total delta 的 58.6%， 而 14B 的 L0 heads 仅占 41%——48 层分摊了 sensitivity。t₁/t₅=0.63（<0.70）， 表面看满足 Spread 两个条件。但实际上 14B 的 \\\"spread\\\" 是 illusory： L0 heads 的 cross-bitwidth gradient 比 7B 弱（top1 delta=3.81 vs 7B 的 6.74）， 且 sensitivity 在 L0-L3 多层间分散而非集中在 L0 单层。 这是一种 \\\"diluted spread\\\"——diagnostic 判定为 Spread 但 MCKP 无法有效利用。\\n\"\n59\t  },\n60\t  {\n61\t    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Constrained MCKP\",\n62\t    \"description\": \"基于 14B hires profiling 跑 constrained MCKP（k=8），评估 PPL。 如果 improvement ≈0%，则 diagnostic 出现 false positive。\\n\",\n63\t    \"results\": {\n64\t      \"qwen14b_baseline_ppl\": 5.84,\n65\t      \"qwen14b_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.02,\n66\t      \"qwen14b_mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 6.94,\n67\t      \"qwen14b_mckp_improvement_over_uniform_pct\": 1.2,\n68\t      \"qwen14b_mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 8.41,\n69\t      \"qwen14b_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.44,\n70\t      \"qwen14b_bit_distribution\": {\n71\t        \"2\": 8,\n72\t        \"4\": 372,\n73\t        \"8\": 4\n74\t      },\n75\t      \"qwen14b_greedy_constrained_ppl\": 6.94,\n76\t      \"qwen14b_solver_equivalence_delta\": 0.0,\n77\t      \"decision_rule_accuracy_6models\": 5,\n78\t      \"decision_rule_total_models\": 6,\n79\t      \"false_positive_model\": \"Qwen2.5-14B\"\n80\t    },\n81\t    \"tables\": [\n82\t      {\n83\t        \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Allocation Results\",\n84\t        \"columns\": [\n85\t          \"method\",\n86\t          \"ppl\",\n87\t          \"compression\",\n88\t          \"vs_uniform\"\n89\t        ],\n90\t        \"rows\": [\n91\t          [\n92\t            \"baseline bf16\",\n93\t            5.84,\n94\t            \"1×\",\n95\t            \"—\"\n96\t          ],\n97\t          [\n98\t            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n99\t            7.02,\n100\t            \"4×\",\n101\t            \"baseline\"\n102\t          ],\n103\t          [\n104\t            \"constrained MCKP k=8\",\n105\t            6.94,\n106\t            \"4×\",\n107\t            \"+1.2%\"\n108\t          ],\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"unconstrained MCKP\",\n111\t            8.41,\n112\t            \"4×\",\n113\t            \"-19.8%\"\n114\t          ],\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"constrained greedy k=8\",\n117\t            6.94,\n118\t            \"4×\",\n119\t            \"+1.2%\"\n120\t          ]\n121\t        ]\n122\t      },\n123\t      {\n124\t        \"name\": \"Decision Rule Accuracy (6 Models)\",\n125\t        \"columns\": [\n126\t          \"model\",\n127\t          \"concentration\",\n128\t          \"t1_t5\",\n129\t          \"diagnostic_prediction\",\n130\t          \"actual_benefit\",\n131\t          \"correct\"\n132\t        ],\n133\t        \"rows\": [\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n136\t            0.61,\n137\t            0.57,\n138\t            \"Spread\",\n139\t            \"+27.3%\",\n140\t            \"✅\"\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n144\t            0.55,\n145\t            0.63,\n146\t            \"Spread\",\n147\t            \"+1.2%\",\n148\t            \"❌ FP\"\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"Yi-1.5-9B\",\n152\t            0.71,\n153\t            0.9,\n154\t            \"Spike\",\n155\t            \"≈0%\",\n156\t            \"✅\"\n157\t          ],\n158\t          [\n159\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n160\t            0.57,\n161\t            0.71,\n162\t            \"Spike\",\n163\t            \"+0.2%\",\n164\t            \"✅\"\n165\t          ],\n166\t          [\n167\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n168\t            0.24,\n169\t            0.18,\n170\t            \"Flat\",\n171\t            \"-0.4%\",\n172\t            \"✅\"\n173\t          ],\n174\t          [\n175\t            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n176\t            0.23,\n177\t            0.38,\n178\t            \"Flat\",\n179\t            \"-0.3%\",\n180\t            \"✅\"\n181\t          ]\n182\t        ]\n183\t      }\n184\t    ],\n185\t    \"figures\": [],\n186\t    \"analysis\": \"Qwen14B 是 diagnostic 的致命反例：同一模型族（Qwen），同一 GQA ratio（7:1）， concentration 和 t₁/t₅ 都满足 Spread 条件，但 MCKP 改进仅 1.2%。 根本原因是 more layers dilute sensitivity，使得 per-head allocation 无法 exploit  sufficient heterogeneity。这说明 diagnostic 缺少第三个维度：total_kv_heads 或 layer_count。 但增加维度后 N=6 的样本量完全不足以 fit 三维 boundary。 Decision rule 降至 5/6 且 failure 发生在 high-confidence prediction（both metrics pass）， 这不是 borderline miss 而是 systematic failure — 严重削弱 diagnostic claim。\\n\\n\\nMCKP constrained PPL=6.94 vs uniform=7.02，improvement 仅 +1.2%（0.08 PPL gap）。 对比 Qwen7B 的 +27.3%（4.53 PPL gap），14B 的 improvement 在噪声范围内。 原因：14B 有 384 heads，每个 head 承载的 information 更少（head_dim 同为 128，但 48 层分摊）， 2-bit 降级的 per-head cost 更小。MCKP 将 L0 的 4 heads 分配到 8-bit，但这仅节省了 total budget 的很小部分——384 heads 中 4 个 8-bit heads 的 budget 释放被稀释到其余 380 heads， 每个 head 只多获得 ~0.01 bit，不足以改变 bit-width assignment。 Unconstrained ratio=1.44×（类似 Gemma-2 的 1.47×），solver 将 ~80 heads 分配到 2-bit， 产生 moderate 而非 catastrophic degradation。 Decision rule accuracy 从 5/5 降至 5/6：14B 是 false positive（diagnostic 预测 benefit，实际无）。\\n\"\n187\t  },\n188\t  {\n189\t    \"name\": \"Gemma-2 Constrained MCKP with BOS Fix\",\n190\t    \"description\": \"用 sliding_window + BOS prepend 修正 eval，重测 Gemma-2 constrained MCKP 和 unconstrained baselines。 BOS bug 可能导致之前的 1.47× unconstrained ratio 和 -0.3% constrained delta 不准确。\\n\",\n191\t    \"results\": {\n192\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_baseline_ppl\": 6.03,\n193\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 6.17,\n194\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_mckp_ppl\": 6.22,\n195\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_vs_uniform_pct\": -0.8,\n196\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_unconstrained_greedy_ppl\": 7.38,\n197\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.22,\n198\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_n2bit_unconstrained\": 106,\n199\t      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_bit_dist\": {\n200\t        \"2\": 8,\n201\t        \"4\": 324,\n202\t        \"8\": 4\n203\t      },\n204\t      \"gemma2_old_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.47,\n205\t      \"gemma2_ratio_shift\": -0.25\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      {\n209\t        \"name\": \"Gemma-2 BOS Fix Impact\",\n210\t        \"columns\": [\n211\t          \"metric\",\n212\t          \"before_bos_fix\",\n213\t          \"after_bos_fix\",\n214\t          \"delta\"\n215\t        ],\n216\t        \"rows\": [\n217\t          [\n218\t            \"baseline PPL\",\n219\t            \"711.6 (buggy) / 6.03 (corrected)\",\n220\t            6.03,\n221\t            \"—\"\n222\t          ],\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"uniform 4-bit PPL\",\n225\t            6.17,\n226\t            6.17,\n227\t            \"0.00\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"unconstrained ratio\",\n231\t            \"1.47×\",\n232\t            \"1.22×\",\n233\t            \"-0.25×\"\n234\t          ],\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"constrained vs uniform\",\n237\t            \"-0.3%\",\n238\t            \"-0.8%\",\n239\t            \"-0.5pp\"\n240\t          ],\n241\t          [\n242\t            \"2-bit heads (unconstrained)\",\n243\t            106,\n244\t            106,\n245\t            \"0\"\n246\t          ]\n247\t        ]\n248\t      },\n249\t      {\n250\t        \"name\": \"Revised Three-Tier Labels (COLLAPSED)\",\n251\t        \"columns\": [\n252\t          \"tier\",\n253\t          \"ratio_range\",\n254\t          \"models\",\n255\t          \"count\"\n256\t        ],\n257\t        \"rows\": [\n258\t          [\n259\t            \"Catastrophic\",\n260\t            \"≥2.0×\",\n261\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B (3.31×)\",\n262\t            1\n263\t          ],\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"Moderate (EMPTY)\",\n266\t            \"1.25-2.0×\",\n267\t            \"—\",\n268\t            0\n269\t          ],\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"Mild\",\n272\t            \"1.0-1.25×\",\n273\t            \"Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Gemma-2 1.22×\",\n274\t            4\n275\t          ]\n276\t        ]\n277\t      }\n278\t    ],\n279\t    \"figures\": [],\n280\t    \"analysis\": \"三档标签失去 moderate 层：Catastrophic (1 model) + Mild (4 models)， 变成 binary 而非 gradient。原本 \\\"concentration-dependent gradient\\\" 叙事中 Gemma-2 是关键中间证据（flat-high-2bit mechanism），现在该机制的 magnitude  被 BOS bug 虚增。修正后 1.22× 的 over-allocation 仍比 Yi/Llama/Mistral 高， 但 gap 缩小到 0.14-0.15×，可能在 noise 范围内。 论文需要重新校准：要么放弃三档（改用连续变量 regression）， 要么承认 moderate tier 的 evidence 不 robust。\\n\\n\\nBOS fix 降低了 baseline PPL（711.6→6.03 已确认），也降低了 quantized PPL。 关键：BOS bug 对 unconstrained allocation 的影响是 non-uniform 的—— 106 个 2-bit heads 的 joint distortion 在有 BOS token 时部分被 BOS 的 attention mass 吸收 （BOS 通常获得高 attention weight，为后续 token 提供 anchor）， 没有 BOS 时这些 heads 的 distortion 被放大。 修正后 unconstrained ratio 从 1.47× 降至 1.22×，落入 mild 范围（1.07-1.22×）， 与 Yi/Llama/Mistral 的 1.07-1.08× 更接近。 三档标签崩塌：原本 Gemma-2 是 \\\"moderate\\\" 独占，现在没有 moderate 了—— 只有 catastrophic（Qwen7B 3.31×）和 mild（其余 4 个模型 1.07-1.22×）。 Constrained vs uniform 变为 -0.8%（从 -0.3%），方向不变但幅度增大。\\n\"\n281\t  },\n282\t  {\n283\t    \"name\": \"L0 Auto-Discovery (No L0 Exclusion)\",\n284\t    \"description\": \"去掉 L0 exclusion 硬约束，仅保留 max_2bit=8，观察 solver 是否仍将 L0 heads 分配到 8-bit。\\n\",\n285\t    \"results\": {\n286\t      \"qwen7b_no_l0excl_ppl\": 11.23,\n287\t      \"qwen7b_l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 4,\n288\t      \"qwen7b_solver_auto_discovers_l0\": true,\n289\t      \"qwen14b_no_l0excl_ppl\": 6.97,\n290\t      \"qwen14b_l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 2,\n291\t      \"qwen14b_solver_partial_discovery\": true\n292\t    },\n293\t    \"tables\": [\n294\t      {\n295\t        \"name\": \"L0 Auto-Discovery Across Qwen Family\",\n296\t        \"columns\": [\n297\t          \"model\",\n298\t          \"l0_dominance\",\n299\t          \"l0_8bit_heads\",\n300\t          \"total_8bit_budget\",\n301\t          \"ppl\",\n302\t          \"auto_discovery\"\n303\t        ],\n304\t        \"rows\": [\n305\t          [\n306\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n307\t            \"26×\",\n308\t            \"4/4\",\n309\t            4,\n310\t            11.23,\n311\t            \"Full ✅\"\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n315\t            \"8.2×\",\n316\t            \"2/8\",\n317\t            4,\n318\t            6.97,\n319\t            \"Partial ⚠️\"\n320\t          ]\n321\t        ]\n322\t      }\n323\t    ],\n324\t    \"figures\": [],\n325\t    \"analysis\": \"Auto-discovery 在 7B 上完美，在 14B 上部分失败。 Reframed narrative 中这不是 critical：constraint 的价值不依赖 auto-discovery， constraint 的 contribution 是 preventing compounding 而非 discovering structure。\\n\\n\\nQwen7B：solver 从 profiling data 自动将 L0 全部 4 heads 分配到 8-bit（delta 极高，cost-benefit ratio 最优），PPL=11.23 不变。这在 7B 上 works 因为 L0 dominance ratio=26×。 Qwen14B：solver 仅将 L0 的 2/8 heads 分配到 8-bit（L0 dominance ratio 仅 8.2×，不够突出）， 其余 2 个 8-bit 名额给了 L2-L3 的 moderate-delta heads。PPL=6.97（vs constrained 6.94）， 差异很小但说明 14B 的 L0 不再是 unambiguous dominant——auto-discovery 部分失败。\\n\"\n326\t  },\n327\t  {\n328\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Full Pipeline\",\n329\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B (GQA 4:1) 全 pipeline：profile → constrained MCKP → eval。\\n\",\n330\t    \"results\": {\n331\t      \"llama_baseline_ppl\": 8.09,\n332\t      \"llama_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n333\t      \"llama_mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n334\t      \"llama_improvement_pct\": 0.2,\n335\t      \"llama_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.07,\n336\t      \"llama_concentration\": 0.57,\n337\t      \"llama_t1_t5\": 0.71,\n338\t      \"llama_shape\": \"Spike (borderline)\",\n339\t      \"llama_natural_k\": 2\n340\t    },\n341\t    \"tables\": [\n342\t      {\n343\t        \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Results\",\n344\t        \"columns\": [\n345\t          \"method\",\n346\t          \"ppl\",\n347\t          \"compression\",\n348\t          \"vs_uniform\"\n349\t        ],\n350\t        \"rows\": [\n351\t          [\n352\t            \"baseline bf16\",\n353\t            8.09,\n354\t            \"1×\",\n355\t            \"—\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n359\t            8.47,\n360\t            \"4×\",\n361\t            \"baseline\"\n362\t          ],\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"constrained MCKP k=8\",\n365\t            8.45,\n366\t            \"4×\",\n367\t            \"+0.2%\"\n368\t          ],\n369\t          [\n370\t            \"unconstrained\",\n371\t            8.63,\n372\t            \"4×\",\n373\t            \"-1.9%\"\n374\t          ]\n375\t        ]\n376\t      }\n377\t    ],\n378\t    \"figures\": [],\n379\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 在 worst tier 下保持。但 t₁/t₅=0.71 的 borderline 值  使 diagnostic 对 Llama 的分类依赖 ±0.01 的阈值精度——如果阈值设为 0.75， Llama 会被误分为 Spread，增加 false positive 风险。\\n\\n\\nLlama 的 concentration=0.57 接近 0.50 阈值但 t₁/t₅=0.71 刚好超过 0.70， 被分类为 Spike。实际上 MCKP 仅选择 2 个 heads 做 2-bit（natural k=2）， constraint 从不 bind。+0.2% improvement 在 noise 范围内。 在 worst tier 下，Llama 的 borderline t₁/t₅=0.71 使得 diagnostic boundary  的 robustness 受质疑——0.70 是 arbitrary cutoff。\\n\"\n380\t  },\n381\t  {\n382\t    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 Full Pipeline\",\n383\t    \"description\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 全 pipeline，Flat distribution 代表。\\n\",\n384\t    \"results\": {\n385\t      \"mistral_baseline_ppl\": 7.04,\n386\t      \"mistral_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.13,\n387\t      \"mistral_mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.16,\n388\t      \"mistral_improvement_pct\": -0.4,\n389\t      \"mistral_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.08,\n390\t      \"mistral_concentration\": 0.24,\n391\t      \"mistral_t1_t5\": 0.18,\n392\t      \"mistral_shape\": \"Flat\",\n393\t      \"mistral_k_monotonic\": true\n394\t    },\n395\t    \"tables\": [\n396\t      {\n397\t        \"name\": \"Mistral-7B Results\",\n398\t        \"columns\": [\n399\t          \"method\",\n400\t          \"ppl\",\n401\t          \"compression\",\n402\t          \"vs_uniform\"\n403\t        ],\n404\t        \"rows\": [\n405\t          [\n406\t            \"baseline bf16\",\n407\t            7.04,\n408\t            \"1×\",\n409\t            \"—\"\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n413\t            7.13,\n414\t            \"4×\",\n415\t            \"baseline\"\n416\t          ],\n417\t          [\n418\t            \"constrained MCKP k=4\",\n419\t            7.16,\n420\t            \"4×\",\n421\t            \"-0.4%\"\n422\t          ],\n423\t          [\n424\t            \"unconstrained\",\n425\t            7.57,\n426\t            \"4×\",\n427\t            \"-6.2%\"\n428\t          ]\n429\t        ]\n430\t      }\n431\t    ],\n432\t    \"figures\": [],\n433\t    \"analysis\": \"Mistral 是最 clean 的 negative case——profiler signal ≈0， 任何 non-uniform allocation 都 ≤ uniform。在 reframed narrative 中 是 \\\"systematic negative result\\\" 的核心证据之一。\\n\\n\\nMistral concentration=0.24（远低于 0.50），profiler 信号几乎为零。 Constrained MCKP 比 uniform 差 0.4%——solver 分配的 2-bit heads  实际上比 uniform 的 all-4bit 更差。k ablation 单调递增证明  每多一个 2-bit head 都 hurts。在 worst tier 下这是 clean negative， 直接支持 \\\"uniform suffices on flat models\\\" 的叙事。\\n\"\n434\t  },\n435\t  {\n436\t    \"name\": \"Compounding Effect Sweep (Qwen7B)\",\n437\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 上 sweep max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 PPL vs k curve。\\n\",\n438\t    \"results\": {\n439\t      \"qwen_k0_ppl\": 15.45,\n440\t      \"qwen_k4_ppl\": 11.93,\n441\t      \"qwen_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n442\t      \"qwen_k10_ppl\": 11.18,\n443\t      \"qwen_k12_ppl\": 11.21,\n444\t      \"qwen_k16_ppl\": 11.52,\n445\t      \"qwen_k24_ppl\": 13.07,\n446\t      \"qwen_k48_ppl\": 19.84,\n447\t      \"qwen_k75_ppl\": 28.36,\n448\t      \"qwen_k112_ppl\": 36.92,\n449\t      \"elbow_k\": 8,\n450\t      \"curve_shape\": \"U-shape with clear minimum at k≈8-10\"\n451\t    },\n452\t    \"tables\": [\n453\t      {\n454\t        \"name\": \"Compounding Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n455\t        \"columns\": [\n456\t          \"max_2bit_k\",\n457\t          \"ppl\",\n458\t          \"delta_vs_k8\"\n459\t        ],\n460\t        \"rows\": [\n461\t          [\n462\t            0,\n463\t            15.45,\n464\t            \"+37.6%\"\n465\t          ],\n466\t          [\n467\t            4,\n468\t            11.93,\n469\t            \"+6.2%\"\n470\t          ],\n471\t          [\n472\t            8,\n473\t            11.23,\n474\t            \"baseline (optimal)\"\n475\t          ],\n476\t          [\n477\t            12,\n478\t            11.21,\n479\t            \"-0.2%\"\n480\t          ],\n481\t          [\n482\t            16,\n483\t            11.52,\n484\t            \"+2.6%\"\n485\t          ],\n486\t          [\n487\t            24,\n488\t            13.07,\n489\t            \"+16.4%\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            48,\n493\t            19.84,\n494\t            \"+76.7%\"\n495\t          ],\n496\t          [\n497\t            112,\n498\t            36.92,\n499\t            \"+228.8%\"\n500\t          ]\n501\t        ]\n502\t      }\n503\t    ],\n504\t    \"figures\": [],\n505\t    \"analysis\": \"Compounding curve 是 paper 的 core figure 之一，在 Qwen 上有力。 但在 worst tier 下，其意义从 \\\"universal phenomenon\\\" 缩小为 \\\"Spread-model-specific phenomenon\\\"。Reframe:  compounding 的 magnitude 和 shape 是 architecture-dependent， 但 constraint 在所有模型上都是 safe（≤ uniform）。\\n\\n\\nQwen7B 的 compounding curve 有清晰 U-shape：k 太小（budget 浪费在不需要的 higher-bit heads）， k 太大（compounding 恶化）。Optimal k=8-10 对应 L0 cluster 的 head 数量。 这是 Qwen7B 的固有特性，worst tier 不改变此结果。 但 worst tier 的问题是：此 curve 是否跨模型可复现？ Llama/Mistral 的 k-PPL curve 平坦或单调，没有 U-shape—— compounding 的 \\\"dramatic elbow\\\" 是 Spread-specific，不 universal。\\n\"\n506\t  },\n507\t  {\n508\t    \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (Qwen7B, 2×/4×/8×)\",\n509\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 在三种压缩率下 constrained MCKP vs uniform。\\n\",\n510\t    \"results\": {\n511\t      \"qwen_2x_uniform_ppl\": 10.07,\n512\t      \"qwen_2x_mckp_ppl\": 9.89,\n513\t      \"qwen_2x_improvement_pct\": 1.8,\n514\t      \"qwen_4x_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n515\t      \"qwen_4x_mckp_ppl\": 11.23,\n516\t      \"qwen_4x_improvement_pct\": 27.3,\n517\t      \"qwen_8x_uniform_ppl\": 2644.0,\n518\t      \"qwen_8x_mckp_ppl\": 42.6,\n519\t      \"qwen_8x_improvement_pct\": 98.4\n520\t    },\n521\t    \"tables\": [\n522\t      {\n523\t        \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n524\t        \"columns\": [\n525\t          \"compression\",\n526\t          \"uniform_ppl\",\n527\t          \"mckp_ppl\",\n528\t          \"improvement\"\n529\t        ],\n530\t        \"rows\": [\n531\t          [\n532\t            \"2× (0.50)\",\n533\t            10.07,\n534\t            9.89,\n535\t            \"+1.8%\"\n536\t          ],\n537\t          [\n538\t            \"4× (0.25)\",\n539\t            15.45,\n540\t            11.23,\n541\t            \"+27.3%\"\n542\t          ],\n543\t          [\n544\t            \"8× (0.125)\",\n545\t            2644.0,\n546\t            42.6,\n547\t            \"+98.4%\"\n548\t          ]\n549\t        ]\n550\t      }\n551\t    ],\n552\t    \"figures\": [],\n553\t    \"analysis\": \"Budget sweep 在 Qwen 上 compelling。Reframe under worst tier: aggressive compression（5.3×+）即使在 non-Spread 模型上也有 cardinality constraint  的价值（Llama 5.3×: 57.60 vs 2644）——constraint 在极端场景下 universally 有用。\\n\\n\\n2× 压缩：budget 充裕（avg 8-bit），大部分 heads 在安全区，仅 1.8% 改进。 4× 是 sweet spot（27.3%），与已有结果一致。 8× 极端压缩下 uniform = all 2-bit（PPL 2644），constrained MCKP 保护 critical heads 大幅降低 PPL（42.6），但绝对质量仍很差。 Worst tier 不改变 Qwen7B 数字，但 cross-model budget sweep （如果做的话）会显示 Llama/Mistral 在 2× 和 4× 都无 improvement。\\n\"\n554\t  },\n555\t  {\n556\t    \"name\": \"High-Resolution Profiling (Qwen7B)\",\n557\t    \"description\": \"64 seq × 2048 tokens hires profiling，重跑 MCKP。\\n\",\n558\t    \"results\": {\n559\t      \"hires_constrained_ppl\": 10.91,\n560\t      \"lowres_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n561\t      \"hires_improvement_over_lowres_pct\": 2.8,\n562\t      \"hires_nonzero_2bit\": 100,\n563\t      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit\": 37,\n564\t      \"hires_profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n565\t      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8\n566\t    },\n567\t    \"tables\": [\n568\t      {\n569\t        \"name\": \"Profiling Resolution Comparison\",\n570\t        \"columns\": [\n571\t          \"resolution\",\n572\t          \"nonzero_heads\",\n573\t          \"constrained_ppl\",\n574\t          \"time_min\"\n575\t        ],\n576\t        \"rows\": [\n577\t          [\n578\t            \"16×512 (lowres)\",\n579\t            37,\n580\t            11.23,\n581\t            \"~10\"\n582\t          ],\n583\t          [\n584\t            \"64×2048 (hires)\",\n585\t            100,\n586\t            10.91,\n587\t            65.5\n588\t          ]\n589\t        ]\n590\t      }\n591\t    ],\n592\t    \"figures\": [],\n593\t    \"analysis\": \"Hires 提供 modest improvement，但 profiling cost 6× 增加。 在 reframed narrative 中，hires vs lowres 是 secondary concern—— constraint 的 contribution 不依赖 profiling resolution。\\n\\n\\nHires profiling 发现更多 non-zero 2-bit delta heads（100 vs 37）， 改善 MCKP allocation（PPL 10.91 vs 11.23，+2.8%）。 8 个 heads 的 allocation 改变（从 4-bit 到 2-bit 或反向）， 说明 lowres 有 ~7% 的 misallocation。 在 worst tier 下，hires 对 Qwen7B 有 modest benefit， 但对 non-Spread 模型（Llama hires: 8.45 vs 8.50）几乎无差。 且 hires profiling 耗时 65 min（vs lowres ~10 min）， cost/benefit ratio 在非 Spread 模型上 unjustified。\\n\"\n594\t  },\n595\t  {\n596\t    \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset Evaluation (Qwen7B)\",\n597\t    \"description\": \"C4 calibration + WikiText-2 evaluation，测试跨 dataset robustness。\\n\",\n598\t    \"results\": {\n599\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n600\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n601\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_improvement_pct\": 26.9,\n602\t      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n603\t      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n604\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n605\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42\n606\t    },\n607\t    \"tables\": [\n608\t      {\n609\t        \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n610\t        \"columns\": [\n611\t          \"calibration\",\n612\t          \"eval\",\n613\t          \"mckp_ppl\",\n614\t          \"uniform_ppl\",\n615\t          \"improvement\"\n616\t        ],\n617\t        \"rows\": [\n618\t          [\n619\t            \"WikiText-2\",\n620\t            \"WikiText-2\",\n621\t            11.29,\n622\t            15.45,\n623\t            \"26.9%\"\n624\t          ],\n625\t          [\n626\t            \"C4\",\n627\t            \"WikiText-2\",\n628\t            11.29,\n629\t            15.45,\n630\t            \"26.9%\"\n631\t          ],\n632\t          [\n633\t            \"WikiText-2\",\n634\t            \"C4\",\n635\t            20.56,\n636\t            35.42,\n637\t            \"42.0%\"\n638\t          ]\n639\t        ]\n640\t      }\n641\t    ],\n642\t    \"figures\": [],\n643\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-dataset robustness 在 Qwen7B 上 strong（L0 dominance 使得 allocation 稳定）。 但这不 extend 到 non-Spread 模型或 14B（where L0 is less dominant）。\\n\\n\\nAllocation agreement 96.4% 说明 calibration source 对 Qwen7B 影响很小 （112 heads 中仅 4 个 disagree）。这是 因为 L0 的 extreme dominance  在任何 distribution 上都一致——agreement 本质上是 \\\"L0 is always dominant\\\"。 Cross-domain PPL（20.56）比 same-domain（11.29）高很多， 但 vs uniform 仍有大幅改善（20.56 vs 35.42）。 Worst tier 的问题：14B 上 agreement 可能更低（L0 dominance 弱， mid-layer allocation 更 distribution-dependent）。\\n\"\n644\t  },\n645\t  {\n646\t    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy Comparison\",\n647\t    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy (Algorithm 1) on {2,4,8,16} vs constrained MCKP。\\n\",\n648\t    \"results\": {\n649\t      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n650\t      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n651\t      \"greedy_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n652\t      \"mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n653\t      \"greedy_constrained_delta_vs_mckp\": 0.0012,\n654\t      \"bit_distribution\": {\n655\t        \"2\": 8,\n656\t        \"4\": 100,\n657\t        \"8\": 4\n658\t      }\n659\t    },\n660\t    \"tables\": [\n661\t      {\n662\t        \"name\": \"Solver Comparison (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n663\t        \"columns\": [\n664\t          \"method\",\n665\t          \"unconstrained_ppl\",\n666\t          \"constrained_k8_ppl\"\n667\t        ],\n668\t        \"rows\": [\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"RateQuant Greedy\",\n671\t            32.45,\n672\t            11.23\n673\t          ],\n674\t          [\n675\t            \"MCKP\",\n676\t            36.92,\n677\t            11.23\n678\t          ],\n679\t          [\n680\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n681\t            \"—\",\n682\t            15.45\n683\t          ]\n684\t        ]\n685\t      }\n686\t    ],\n687\t    \"figures\": [],\n688\t    \"analysis\": \"Solver equivalence under constraint 是 robust result，在 worst tier 下 成为 paper 的 core contribution 之一（不依赖 diagnostic）。\\n\\n\\nUnconstrained greedy (32.45) 和 MCKP (36.92) 都 catastrophically fail。 Constrained 后两者 converge（Δ=0.0012 ≈ 0）。 这是 \\\"constraint is the contribution, not the solver\\\" 的 strongest evidence。 Worst tier 不改变此结论——solver equivalence under constraint  是 Qwen7B 的数学属性（constrained feasible set small enough）， 无论 diagnostic 是否成立。\\n\"\n689\t  },\n690\t  {\n691\t    \"name\": \"Oracle Comparison (Brute-Force Subset)\",\n692\t    \"description\": \"Qwen7B 3-4 layer groups 上 brute-force optimal vs MCKP。\\n\",\n693\t    \"results\": {\n694\t      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n695\t      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0183,\n696\t      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0046,\n697\t      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n698\t      \"gap_nature\": \"2-bit head position swap within same bit budget\"\n699\t    },\n700\t    \"tables\": [\n701\t      {\n702\t        \"name\": \"Oracle vs MCKP (Qwen2.5-7B Subset)\",\n703\t        \"columns\": [\n704\t          \"layer_group\",\n705\t          \"mckp_ppl\",\n706\t          \"oracle_ppl\",\n707\t          \"gap\"\n708\t        ],\n709\t        \"rows\": [\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"L0-L3\",\n712\t            10.91,\n713\t            10.91,\n714\t            0.0\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            \"L1\",\n718\t            \"—\",\n719\t            \"—\",\n720\t            0.0183\n721\t          ],\n722\t          [\n723\t            \"L4\",\n724\t            \"—\",\n725\t            \"—\",\n726\t            0.0045\n727\t          ],\n728\t          [\n729\t            \"L11\",\n730\t            \"—\",\n731\t            \"—\",\n732\t            0.0136\n733\t          ]\n734\t        ]\n735\t      }\n736\t    ],\n737\t    \"figures\": [],\n738\t    \"analysis\": \"Near-optimality 是 standalone result，加强 constraint contribution。\\n\\n\\nMCKP gap to oracle 极小（max 0.0183 PPL），5/8 layers 完全 optimal。 Gap 来源：3 个 layer 上 MCKP 选了 slightly suboptimal 的 2-bit head 位置， 但 bit budget 完全相同——差异仅在 which head gets 2-bit，非结构性错误。 即使在 worst tier 下，MCKP near-optimality 成立——这不依赖 diagnostic。\\n\"\n739\t  },\n740\t  {\n741\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Domain Calibration Robustness\",\n742\t    \"description\": \"C4 calibrate / WikiText-2 evaluate 及反向，报告 allocation agreement。\\n\",\n743\t    \"results\": {\n744\t      \"qwen_agreement\": 0.964,\n745\t      \"llama_agreement\": 0.977,\n746\t      \"mistral_agreement\": 0.965,\n747\t      \"qwen14b_predicted_agreement\": 0.88\n748\t    },\n749\t    \"tables\": [\n750\t      {\n751\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Calibration Agreement\",\n752\t        \"columns\": [\n753\t          \"model\",\n754\t          \"agreement\",\n755\t          \"heads_agree\",\n756\t          \"total\"\n757\t        ],\n758\t        \"rows\": [\n759\t          [\n760\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n761\t            \"96.4%\",\n762\t            108,\n763\t            112\n764\t          ],\n765\t          [\n766\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n767\t            \"97.7%\",\n768\t            250,\n769\t            256\n770\t          ],\n771\t          [\n772\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n773\t            \"96.5%\",\n774\t            247,\n775\t            256\n776\t          ],\n777\t          [\n778\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B (predicted)\",\n779\t            \"~88%\",\n780\t            \"~338\",\n781\t            384\n782\t          ]\n783\t        ]\n784\t      }\n785\t    ],\n786\t    \"figures\": [],\n787\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-calibration robustness 在小模型上 strong， 但可能不 scale to larger models（more heads → more ambiguity）。\\n\\n\\n三个 7-9B 模型都有 >96% agreement，说明 calibration robust。 但 worst tier 预测 Qwen14B 的 agreement 可能降至 ~88%， 因为 14B 的 sensitivity 更分散、mid-layer heads 的 ranking  更 distribution-dependent。这削弱 \\\"one-shot calibration\\\" 的 practicality claim。\\n\"\n788\t  },\n789\t  {\n790\t    \"name\": \"Head Sensitivity Visualization\",\n791\t    \"description\": \"Paper-quality figures: per-head delta heatmap, compounding curve, allocation comparison。\\n\",\n792\t    \"results\": {\n793\t      \"figures_generated\": 5,\n794\t      \"key_visual\": \"5-model heatmap comparison shows architecture diversity\",\n795\t      \"worst_tier_impact\": \"14B heatmap looks like diluted version of 7B, weakens family consistency\"\n796\t    },\n797\t    \"tables\": [],\n798\t    \"figures\": [],\n799\t    \"analysis\": \"Visualization 诚实展示 diagnostic 的 limitation 反而增加 credibility。 14B false positive 在 scatter plot 上是 visible anomaly，需要 explicit 讨论。\\n\\n\\nVisualization 不产生新数据但在 worst tier 下需要更新： (1) 加入 14B heatmap 显示 diluted spread pattern（与 7B 对比削弱 Qwen family story） (2) 三档 gradient bar chart 中 moderate 消失（Gemma-2 BOS fix） (3) Decision rule scatter 中 14B 落在 Spread 象限但标记为 false positive\\n\"\n800\t  },\n801\t  {\n802\t    \"name\": \"Downstream Task Evaluation (Qwen7B)\",\n803\t    \"description\": \"ARC-C / HellaSwag / PIQA / WinoGrande on Qwen7B + 4 non-Spread models at 4×。\\n\",\n804\t    \"results\": {\n805\t      \"qwen_avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n806\t      \"qwen_arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n807\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n808\t      \"yi_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.77,\n809\t      \"llama_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.99,\n810\t      \"mistral_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.48,\n811\t      \"gemma2_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": 0.14,\n812\t      \"qwen14b_predicted_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.2\n813\t    },\n814\t    \"tables\": [\n815\t      {\n816\t        \"name\": \"Downstream Summary (6 Models)\",\n817\t        \"columns\": [\n818\t          \"model\",\n819\t          \"shape\",\n820\t          \"mckp_vs_uniform_pp\",\n821\t          \"diagnostic_correct\"\n822\t        ],\n823\t        \"rows\": [\n824\t          [\n825\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n826\t            \"Spread\",\n827\t            \"+2.60pp\",\n828\t            \"✅\"\n829\t          ],\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n832\t            \"Diluted Spread\",\n833\t            \"-0.2pp (noise)\",\n834\t            \"❌ FP\"\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"Yi-1.5-9B\",\n838\t            \"Spike\",\n839\t            \"-0.77pp\",\n840\t            \"✅\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n844\t            \"Spike\",\n845\t            \"-0.99pp\",\n846\t            \"✅\"\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n850\t            \"Flat\",\n851\t            \"-0.48pp\",\n852\t            \"✅\"\n853\t          ],\n854\t          [\n855\t            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n856\t            \"Flat\",\n857\t            \"+0.14pp (noise)\",\n858\t            \"✅\"\n859\t          ]\n860\t        ]\n861\t      }\n862\t    ],\n863\t    \"figures\": [],\n864\t    \"analysis\": \"Downstream data 在 worst tier 下 reinforces \\\"1/6 models benefit\\\"—— 更适合 framing 为 systematic negative result + one strong positive case study。\\n\\n\\n5-model downstream data 完整，结果与 PPL 一致。 Worst tier 预测 Qwen14B downstream：MCKP vs uniform ≈ -0.2pp（与 PPL 的 +1.2% 不一致方向？ 不，PPL improvement +1.2% 意味着 MCKP 稍好，downstream 可能 +0.1-0.3pp 或 noise）。 但 14B 的 downstream 数据不足以区分 signal vs noise（无 multi-seed CI）。 论文需报告 14B 但不能 claim benefit。\\n\"\n865\t  },\n866\t  {\n867\t    \"name\": \"70B Profiling-Only (Qwen2.5-72B)\",\n868\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B distortion profiling（不做 eval），分析 sensitivity 是否随 model size 缩放。\\n\",\n869\t    \"results\": {\n870\t      \"qwen72b_concentration\": 0.48,\n871\t      \"qwen72b_t1_t5\": 0.69,\n872\t      \"qwen72b_l0_dominance_ratio\": 5.1,\n873\t      \"qwen72b_total_heads\": 640,\n874\t      \"qwen72b_diagnostic_prediction\": \"borderline (conc<0.50)\"\n875\t    },\n876\t    \"tables\": [\n877\t      {\n878\t        \"name\": \"Qwen Family Scaling\",\n879\t        \"columns\": [\n880\t          \"model\",\n881\t          \"params\",\n882\t          \"layers\",\n883\t          \"kv_heads\",\n884\t          \"concentration\",\n885\t          \"t1_t5\",\n886\t          \"predicted_shape\"\n887\t        ],\n888\t        \"rows\": [\n889\t          [\n890\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n891\t            \"7B\",\n892\t            28,\n893\t            112,\n894\t            0.61,\n895\t            0.57,\n896\t            \"Spread\"\n897\t          ],\n898\t          [\n899\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n900\t            \"14B\",\n901\t            48,\n902\t            384,\n903\t            0.55,\n904\t            0.63,\n905\t            \"Diluted Spread\"\n906\t          ],\n907\t          [\n908\t            \"Qwen2.5-72B\",\n909\t            \"72B\",\n910\t            80,\n911\t            640,\n912\t            0.48,\n913\t            0.69,\n914\t            \"Borderline/Flat\"\n915\t          ]\n916\t        ]\n917\t      }\n918\t    ],\n919\t    \"figures\": [],\n920\t    \"analysis\": \"如果 72B profiling 证实 concentration < 0.50，则 Spread pattern  不是 Qwen architecture 的固有属性而是 small-model artifact。 这对 diagnostic 的 practical value 是致命打击—— practitioner 最关心的 large models 恰恰最不可能是 Spread。\\n\\n\\n72B 有 80 layers × 8 KV heads = 640 heads。更多层进一步稀释 concentration。 Concentration=0.48（刚低于 0.50 阈值），t₁/t₅=0.69（刚低于 0.70）。 Diagnostic 预测 borderline/Flat——如果确实如此， 则 Qwen 模型族呈现 \\\"7B=Spread, 14B=Diluted Spread, 72B=Flat\\\" 的递减梯度， 说明 model size increase 系统性地 dilute sensitivity concentration。 这直接挑战 \\\"Qwen family is Spread\\\" 的 assumption。\\n\"\n921\t  },\n922\t  {\n923\t    \"name\": \"K/V Separation\",\n924\t    \"description\": \"将 K 和 V heads 作为独立 MCKP items，允许 asymmetric K/V budget。\\n\",\n925\t    \"results\": {\n926\t      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n927\t      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n928\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n929\t      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.31,\n930\t      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n931\t      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true\n932\t    },\n933\t    \"tables\": [\n934\t      {\n935\t        \"name\": \"K/V Separation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n936\t        \"columns\": [\n937\t          \"method\",\n938\t          \"ppl\",\n939\t          \"k_2bit\",\n940\t          \"v_2bit\",\n941\t          \"vs_joint\"\n942\t        ],\n943\t        \"rows\": [\n944\t          [\n945\t            \"Joint K+V\",\n946\t            10.91,\n947\t            4,\n948\t            4,\n949\t            \"baseline\"\n950\t          ],\n951\t          [\n952\t            \"K/V separated\",\n953\t            11.22,\n954\t            16,\n955\t            0,\n956\t            \"+2.8%\"\n957\t          ],\n958\t          [\n959\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n960\t            15.45,\n961\t            0,\n962\t            0,\n963\t            \"+41.6%\"\n964\t          ]\n965\t        ]\n966\t      }\n967\t    ],\n968\t    \"figures\": [],\n969\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative result：K/V separation 不如 joint optimization。 论文用 1 paragraph 报告，作为 RateQuant comparison 的补充。\\n\\n\\nK/V separation 让 solver 独立优化 K 和 V 的 budget。 结果：V heads 全部 4-bit（sensitivity 低），K heads 有 16 个 2-bit（budget 被 V 让渡）。 但 PPL 11.22 略差于 joint optimization 的 10.91（Δ=0.31）， 因为 K-only 2-bit 的 compounding 比 joint 分配更 aggressive。 在 worst tier 下，这是 negative result——joint optimization 优于 separation， 说明 K/V interaction matters，简单的 asymmetric budget 不够。\\n\"\n970\t  },\n971\t  {\n972\t    \"name\": \"L0-Only Heuristic Baseline\",\n973\t    \"description\": \"最简单的 non-uniform 策略：L0 全部 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit。 如果匹配 MCKP，则 full optimization 不必要。\\n\",\n974\t    \"results\": {\n975\t      \"qwen_l0_random_mean\": 11.69,\n976\t      \"qwen_l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n977\t      \"qwen_l0_random_std\": 0.47,\n978\t      \"qwen_naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n979\t      \"qwen_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n980\t      \"llama_l0_random_mean\": 10.48,\n981\t      \"llama_mckp_ppl\": 8.45,\n982\t      \"mistral_l0_random_mean\": 7.56,\n983\t      \"mistral_mckp_ppl\": 7.16\n984\t    },\n985\t    \"tables\": [\n986\t      {\n987\t        \"name\": \"L0 Heuristic vs MCKP\",\n988\t        \"columns\": [\n989\t          \"model\",\n990\t          \"l0_random_median\",\n991\t          \"mckp\",\n992\t          \"uniform\",\n993\t          \"mckp_vs_heuristic_gap\"\n994\t        ],\n995\t        \"rows\": [\n996\t          [\n997\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n998\t            11.52,\n999\t            10.91,\n1000\t            15.45,\n1001\t            \"5.6%\"\n1002\t          ],\n1003\t          [\n1004\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n1005\t            10.04,\n1006\t            8.45,\n1007\t            8.47,\n1008\t            \"18.8%\"\n1009\t          ],\n1010\t          [\n1011\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n1012\t            7.59,\n1013\t            7.16,\n1014\t            7.13,\n1015\t            \"6.0%\"\n1016\t          ]\n1017\t        ]\n1018\t      }\n1019\t    ],\n1020\t    \"figures\": [],\n1021\t    \"analysis\": \"MCKP outperforms heuristic on all models，但 gap varies。 在 non-Spread models，MCKP 和 heuristic 都 ≤ uniform—— the right choice is \\\"don't bother\\\" rather than \\\"optimize better\\\"。\\n\\n\\nL0-random heuristic（随机选 k 个 non-L0 heads 做 2-bit）在 Qwen 上 median=11.52 vs MCKP=10.91（gap 5.6%）。MCKP 的优势来自  precisely 选择 which non-L0 heads 做 2-bit（vs random）。 在 Llama/Mistral 上 L0-random 显著差于 MCKP（且 MCKP ≈ uniform）， 说明 heuristic 不是 universal substitute。 Worst tier 的 concern：14B 上 L0-random 可能 ≈ MCKP（因为 14B 的 MCKP 本身 ≈ uniform）， 进一步削弱 MCKP 的 value proposition。\\n\"\n1022\t  },\n1023\t  {\n1024\t    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy + Cardinality Constraint\",\n1025\t    \"description\": \"验证 constraint 是否是 key contribution（vs solver choice）。 Greedy + k=8 vs MCKP + k=8 vs both unconstrained。\\n\",\n1026\t    \"results\": {\n1027\t      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n1028\t      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n1029\t      \"greedy_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n1030\t      \"mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n1031\t      \"delta_greedy_vs_mckp_constrained\": 0.0012,\n1032\t      \"solver_equivalence\": true\n1033\t    },\n1034\t    \"tables\": [\n1035\t      {\n1036\t        \"name\": \"Solver Equivalence Under Constraint\",\n1037\t        \"columns\": [\n1038\t          \"method\",\n1039\t          \"unconstrained\",\n1040\t          \"constrained_k8\",\n1041\t          \"delta\"\n1042\t        ],\n1043\t        \"rows\": [\n1044\t          [\n1045\t            \"RateQuant Greedy\",\n1046\t            32.45,\n1047\t            11.23,\n1048\t            \"—\"\n1049\t          ],\n1050\t          [\n1051\t            \"MCKP\",\n1052\t            36.92,\n1053\t            11.23,\n1054\t            \"Δ=0.0012\"\n1055\t          ]\n1056\t        ]\n1057\t      }\n1058\t    ],\n1059\t    \"figures\": [],\n1060\t    \"analysis\": \"在 reframed worst-tier narrative 中，solver equivalence under constraint  成为 Claim 1 的 core evidence。不需要 diagnostic 来 motivate。\\n\\n\\nCore finding：constraint 使 greedy = MCKP（Δ=0.0012 ≈ 0）。 Constrained feasible set 小到 greedy 的 local search 等于 global optimum。 这是 paper 最 robust 的 result——不依赖 diagnostic，不依赖 model choice， 纯数学属性。在 worst tier 下这是 anchor result。\\n\"\n1061\t  },\n1062\t  {\n1063\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Error Bars (Qwen7B)\",\n1064\t    \"description\": \"3 个 calibration seed 的 constrained MCKP，报告 mean±std。\\n\",\n1065\t    \"results\": {\n1066\t      \"mckp_seed0\": 11.02,\n1067\t      \"mckp_seed1\": 10.9,\n1068\t      \"mckp_seed2\": 11.05,\n1069\t      \"mckp_mean\": 10.99,\n1070\t      \"mckp_std\": 0.065,\n1071\t      \"uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n1072\t      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n1073\t      \"bit_dist_all_seeds\": \"2:8, 4:100, 8:4\"\n1074\t    },\n1075\t    \"tables\": [\n1076\t      {\n1077\t        \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Results (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n1078\t        \"columns\": [\n1079\t          \"seed\",\n1080\t          \"mckp_ppl\",\n1081\t          \"bit_dist\",\n1082\t          \"agreement_with_seed0\"\n1083\t        ],\n1084\t        \"rows\": [\n1085\t          [\n1086\t            \"seed_0\",\n1087\t            11.02,\n1088\t            \"8:100:4\",\n1089\t            \"—\"\n1090\t          ],\n1091\t          [\n1092\t            \"seed_1\",\n1093\t            10.9,\n1094\t            \"8:100:4\",\n1095\t            \"94.6%\"\n1096\t          ],\n1097\t          [\n1098\t            \"seed_2\",\n1099\t            11.05,\n1100\t            \"8:100:4\",\n1101\t            \"91.1%\"\n1102\t          ],\n1103\t          [\n1104\t            \"mean±std\",\n1105\t            \"10.99±0.065\",\n1106\t            \"—\",\n1107\t            \"—\"\n1108\t          ]\n1109\t        ]\n1110\t      }\n1111\t    ],\n1112\t    \"figures\": [],\n1113\t    \"analysis\": \"Qwen7B 的 statistical robustness 是 solid。但 N=3 seeds 仍然 limited。 论文应报告 \\\"our main result is robust to calibration variation\\\" 但  not claim \\\"statistical significance\\\" formally。\\n\\n\\n三个 seed 的 MCKP PPL std=0.065（mean=10.99），95% CI = [10.86, 11.12]。 与 uniform 的 gap（15.45 - 10.99 = 4.46）远大于 CI width（0.26）， Qwen7B 上的 improvement 是 statistically robust。 Bit distribution 三个 seed 完全一致（8:100:4），allocation agreement 90.2% （head-level 有 10% variation 但 bit-level distribution 不变）。 Worst tier 的 concern：14B 上 std 可能更大（sensitivity 更分散 → calibration noise 更大）， 且 improvement 本身在 noise 范围内。\\n\"\n1114\t  },\n1115\t  {\n1116\t    \"name\": \"Runtime/Latency Benchmark (Qwen7B)\",\n1117\t    \"description\": \"端到端 inference latency 和 throughput。\\n\",\n1118\t    \"results\": {\n1119\t      \"bf16_prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n1120\t      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n1121\t      \"uniform4_prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n1122\t      \"uniform4_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n1123\t      \"mckp_prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n1124\t      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n1125\t      \"mckp_throughput_tok_s\": 21.8,\n1126\t      \"uniform4_throughput_tok_s\": 23.6,\n1127\t      \"mckp_solver_sec\": 0.005,\n1128\t      \"mckp_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 8.5\n1129\t    },\n1130\t    \"tables\": [\n1131\t      {\n1132\t        \"name\": \"Runtime Benchmark (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n1133\t        \"columns\": [\n1134\t          \"config\",\n1135\t          \"prefill_ms\",\n1136\t          \"decode_ms\",\n1137\t          \"throughput\",\n1138\t          \"memory_MB\"\n1139\t        ],\n1140\t        \"rows\": [\n1141\t          [\n1142\t            \"bf16\",\n1143\t            45.86,\n1144\t            33.78,\n1145\t            \"29.6 tok/s\",\n1146\t            21.0\n1147\t          ],\n1148\t          [\n1149\t            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n1150\t            54.25,\n1151\t            42.46,\n1152\t            \"23.6 tok/s\",\n1153\t            5.25\n1154\t          ],\n1155\t          [\n1156\t            \"MCKP constrained\",\n1157\t            57.03,\n1158\t            46.09,\n1159\t            \"21.8 tok/s\",\n1160\t            5.25\n1161\t          ]\n1162\t        ]\n1163\t      }\n1164\t    ],\n1165\t    \"figures\": [],\n1166\t    \"analysis\": \"8.5% latency overhead 是 acceptable trade-off 但仅在 Spread models 上。 Reframe: \\\"if diagnostic uncertain, use uniform 4-bit to avoid latency cost\\\"  — 这与 worst-tier narrative 的 \\\"conservative recommendation\\\" 一致。\\n\\n\\nMixed-precision MCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 慢 ~8.5%（decode 46.09 vs 42.46 ms/tok）， 因为 mixed bit-width 需要 per-head dequantize dispatch（vs uniform 的 vectorized batch dequant）。 内存相同（5.25 MB），solver 本身 negligible（5ms）。 Worst tier 的 concern：8.5% latency overhead 换 PPL improvement 仅在 Qwen7B 上 worth it—— 在 non-Spread 模型上 overhead 仍存在但 PPL 无 improvement， 纯亏损。Reviewer 会问 \\\"when is the latency cost justified?\\\"\\n\"\n1167\t  },\n1168\t  {\n1169\t    \"name\": \"W9 Compounding Scaling (Worst Tier)\",\n1170\t    \"description\": \"Qwen7B 上 top-k vs random-k 2-bit assignment sweep，刻画 super-additivity。\\n\",\n1171\t    \"results\": {\n1172\t      \"k1_topk_ppl\": 9.83,\n1173\t      \"k1_randomk_ppl\": 9.89,\n1174\t      \"k4_topk_ppl\": 9.85,\n1175\t      \"k4_randomk_ppl\": 10.06,\n1176\t      \"k8_topk_ppl\": 10.04,\n1177\t      \"k8_randomk_ppl\": 11.07,\n1178\t      \"k16_topk_ppl\": 10.42,\n1179\t      \"k16_randomk_ppl\": 12.91,\n1180\t      \"k32_topk_ppl\": 11.6,\n1181\t      \"k32_randomk_ppl\": 18.33,\n1182\t      \"k64_topk_ppl\": 22.95,\n1183\t      \"k64_randomk_ppl\": 55.94,\n1184\t      \"k64_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.45,\n1185\t      \"k32_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.58,\n1186\t      \"k16_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.24,\n1187\t      \"non_monotonic_flag\": true,\n1188\t      \"variance_at_k16_masks_trend\": true\n1189\t    },\n1190\t    \"tables\": [\n1191\t      {\n1192\t        \"name\": \"W9 Compounding (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\",\n1193\t        \"columns\": [\n1194\t          \"k\",\n1195\t          \"topk_ppl\",\n1196\t          \"randomk_ppl\",\n1197\t          \"randomk_std\",\n1198\t          \"ratio\",\n1199\t          \"monotonic\"\n1200\t        ],\n1201\t        \"rows\": [\n1202\t          [\n1203\t            1,\n1204\t            9.83,\n1205\t            9.89,\n1206\t            0.05,\n1207\t            1.0,\n1208\t            \"—\"\n1209\t          ],\n1210\t          [\n1211\t            4,\n1212\t            9.85,\n1213\t            10.06,\n1214\t            0.06,\n1215\t            1.24,\n1216\t            \"↑\"\n1217\t          ],\n1218\t          [\n1219\t            8,\n1220\t            10.04,\n1221\t            11.07,\n1222\t            0.69,\n1223\t            1.76,\n1224\t            \"↑\"\n1225\t          ],\n1226\t          [\n1227\t            16,\n1228\t            10.42,\n1229\t            12.91,\n1230\t            0.4,\n1231\t            1.24,\n1232\t            \"↓ ⚠️\"\n1233\t          ],\n1234\t          [\n1235\t            32,\n1236\t            11.6,\n1237\t            18.33,\n1238\t            2.53,\n1239\t            1.58,\n1240\t            \"↑\"\n1241\t          ],\n1242\t          [\n1243\t            64,\n1244\t            22.95,\n1245\t            55.94,\n1246\t            9.73,\n1247\t            1.45,\n1248\t            \"↓ ⚠️\"\n1249\t          ]\n1250\t        ]\n1251\t      }\n1252\t    ],\n1253\t    \"figures\": [],\n1254\t    \"analysis\": \"在 worst tier 下，W9 data 的 non-monotonicity 和 high variance  使得 formal super-additivity claim 不成立。 Reframe: 报告为 \\\"empirical observation of compounding trend with substantial variance\\\"， 不 formalize 为 theorem 或 proposition。 Compounding 的 qualitative story 仍 hold（ratio >1 at all k>1）， 但 quantitative precision 不足以支撑 formal contribution。\\n\\n\\nWorst-tier 下 k=64 的 randomk/topk ratio 降至 1.45（vs 实际 2.44 的 actual data 中位估计）。 k=8-16 区间出现 non-monotonic：k=8 ratio=1.76 但 k=16 ratio 回落到 1.24， 然后 k=32 又升到 1.58。这种 non-monotonicity 可能来自： (1) random-k 的 seed variance（std=0.4-2.5 across seeds）， (2) top-k 在某些 k 值恰好避开 interaction cluster 而 random 没有。 Non-monotonic behavior 使得 \\\"super-additivity monotonically increases with k\\\"  的 clean story 不成立。论文需要 acknowledge variance 并报告 CI。 ratio 的 overall trend 仍是 increasing（1.24→1.45→1.58→1.45）， 但 non-monotonicity at intermediate k 削弱 formalization strength。\\n\"\n1255\t  },\n1256\t  {\n1257\t    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Downstream Eval (Predicted)\",\n1258\t    \"description\": \"如果 14B profiling + MCKP 完成，需跑 downstream eval 验证 PPL 与 downstream 一致性。\\n\",\n1259\t    \"results\": {\n1260\t      \"qwen14b_baseline_avg\": 0.72,\n1261\t      \"qwen14b_uniform_avg\": 0.71,\n1262\t      \"qwen14b_mckp_avg\": 0.71,\n1263\t      \"qwen14b_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": 0.1,\n1264\t      \"qwen14b_arc_challenge_delta_pp\": -0.5,\n1265\t      \"qwen14b_hellaswag_delta_pp\": 0.3\n1266\t    },\n1267\t    \"tables\": [\n1268\t      {\n1269\t        \"name\": \"Qwen14B Downstream (Predicted)\",\n1270\t        \"columns\": [\n1271\t          \"task\",\n1272\t          \"uniform\",\n1273\t          \"mckp\",\n1274\t          \"delta_pp\"\n1275\t        ],\n1276\t        \"rows\": [\n1277\t          [\n1278\t            \"arc_challenge\",\n1279\t            0.58,\n1280\t            0.575,\n1281\t            \"-0.5\"\n1282\t          ],\n1283\t          [\n1284\t            \"hellaswag\",\n1285\t            0.72,\n1286\t            0.723,\n1287\t            \"+0.3\"\n1288\t          ],\n1289\t          [\n1290\t            \"piqa\",\n1291\t            0.81,\n1292\t            0.811,\n1293\t            \"+0.1\"\n1294\t          ],\n1295\t          [\n1296\t            \"winogrande\",\n1297\t            0.73,\n1298\t            0.728,\n1299\t            \"-0.2\"\n1300\t          ],\n1301\t          [\n1302\t            \"average\",\n1303\t            0.71,\n1304\t            0.71,\n1305\t            \"+0.1\"\n1306\t          ]\n1307\t        ]\n1308\t      }\n1309\t    ],\n1310\t    \"figures\": [],\n1311\t    \"analysis\": \"Downstream 确认 14B false positive——不仅 PPL 无 improvement， downstream 也在 noise。论文需要 transparent reporting。\\n\\nPPL improvement +1.2% → downstream ≈ 0pp（noise）。 arc_challenge 可能略负（-0.5pp），与跨模型的 arc_challenge 系统性敏感一致。 hellaswag 略正（+0.3pp）但在 seed noise 范围内。 整体结论：14B downstream 与 PPL 一致——MCKP 无 meaningful benefit。\\n\"\n1312\t  }\n1313\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60b94339-87f0-47ef-aa74-b7c45d2f68d8","uuid":"5462c821-0f6b-4b98-9268-9911ff1d8362","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:54:32.358Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T085855/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Hires Profiling\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B hires bf16 2-bit-only profiling（48 layers × 8 KV heads = 384 heads）。 测试 diagnostic 是否在 Qwen 模型族内泛化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen14b_baseline_ppl\": 5.84,\n      \"qwen14b_top5_concentration\": 0.55,\n      \"qwen14b_t1_t5\": 0.63,\n      \"qwen14b_l0_dominance_ratio\": 8.2,\n      \"qwen14b_top1_head\": \"L0H2\",\n      \"qwen14b_top1_delta_2bit\": 3.81,\n      \"qwen14b_l0_4heads_total_share\": 0.41,\n      \"qwen14b_delta_2bit_cv\": 5.12,\n      \"qwen14b_positive_delta_heads\": 370,\n      \"qwen14b_total_heads\": 384,\n      \"qwen14b_distribution_shape\": \"borderline_spread\",\n      \"diagnostic_prediction\": \"Spread (conc≥0.50 AND t₁/t₅≤0.70)\",\n      \"diagnostic_correct\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Qwen Family Profiling Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"layers\",\n          \"kv_heads\",\n          \"concentration\",\n          \"t1_t5\",\n          \"l0_share\",\n          \"top1_delta\",\n          \"shape\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            28,\n            112,\n            0.61,\n            0.57,\n            \"58.6%\",\n            6.74,\n            \"Spread\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            48,\n            384,\n            0.55,\n            0.63,\n            \"41.0%\",\n            3.81,\n            \"Diluted Spread\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic 两个指标都刚过阈值（concentration 0.55 > 0.50, t₁/t₅ 0.63 < 0.70）， 但边际通过。14B 的关键问题：更多层分摊了 sensitivity，使得 L0 的 dominance 不足以 让 MCKP 产生有意义的 allocation 差异。这暴露了 joint diagnostic 的 boundary fragility—— 阈值在 border 附近不 robust。\\n\\n\\nQwen2.5-14B 有 48 layers × 8 KV heads = 384 heads（vs 7B 的 28×4=112）。 GQA 仍是 7:1，保留 L0 某些 heads 的较高 sensitivity（concentration=0.55，刚过 0.50 阈值）。 但 14B 的 L0 cluster 比 7B 弱得多：7B 的 L0 4 heads 占 total delta 的 58.6%， 而 14B 的 L0 heads 仅占 41%——48 层分摊了 sensitivity。t₁/t₅=0.63（<0.70）， 表面看满足 Spread 两个条件。但实际上 14B 的 \\\"spread\\\" 是 illusory： L0 heads 的 cross-bitwidth gradient 比 7B 弱（top1 delta=3.81 vs 7B 的 6.74）， 且 sensitivity 在 L0-L3 多层间分散而非集中在 L0 单层。 这是一种 \\\"diluted spread\\\"——diagnostic 判定为 Spread 但 MCKP 无法有效利用。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Constrained MCKP\",\n    \"description\": \"基于 14B hires profiling 跑 constrained MCKP（k=8），评估 PPL。 如果 improvement ≈0%，则 diagnostic 出现 false positive。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen14b_baseline_ppl\": 5.84,\n      \"qwen14b_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.02,\n      \"qwen14b_mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 6.94,\n      \"qwen14b_mckp_improvement_over_uniform_pct\": 1.2,\n      \"qwen14b_mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 8.41,\n      \"qwen14b_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.44,\n      \"qwen14b_bit_distribution\": {\n        \"2\": 8,\n        \"4\": 372,\n        \"8\": 4\n      },\n      \"qwen14b_greedy_constrained_ppl\": 6.94,\n      \"qwen14b_solver_equivalence_delta\": 0.0,\n      \"decision_rule_accuracy_6models\": 5,\n      \"decision_rule_total_models\": 6,\n      \"false_positive_model\": \"Qwen2.5-14B\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Allocation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"compression\",\n          \"vs_uniform\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline bf16\",\n            5.84,\n            \"1×\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n            7.02,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"constrained MCKP k=8\",\n            6.94,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"+1.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"unconstrained MCKP\",\n            8.41,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"-19.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"constrained greedy k=8\",\n            6.94,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"+1.2%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Decision Rule Accuracy (6 Models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"concentration\",\n          \"t1_t5\",\n          \"diagnostic_prediction\",\n          \"actual_benefit\",\n          \"correct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            0.61,\n            0.57,\n            \"Spread\",\n            \"+27.3%\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            0.55,\n            0.63,\n            \"Spread\",\n            \"+1.2%\",\n            \"❌ FP\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi-1.5-9B\",\n            0.71,\n            0.9,\n            \"Spike\",\n            \"≈0%\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            0.57,\n            0.71,\n            \"Spike\",\n            \"+0.2%\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            0.24,\n            0.18,\n            \"Flat\",\n            \"-0.4%\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n            0.23,\n            0.38,\n            \"Flat\",\n            \"-0.3%\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Qwen14B 是 diagnostic 的致命反例：同一模型族（Qwen），同一 GQA ratio（7:1）， concentration 和 t₁/t₅ 都满足 Spread 条件，但 MCKP 改进仅 1.2%。 根本原因是 more layers dilute sensitivity，使得 per-head allocation 无法 exploit  sufficient heterogeneity。这说明 diagnostic 缺少第三个维度：total_kv_heads 或 layer_count。 但增加维度后 N=6 的样本量完全不足以 fit 三维 boundary。 Decision rule 降至 5/6 且 failure 发生在 high-confidence prediction（both metrics pass）， 这不是 borderline miss 而是 systematic failure — 严重削弱 diagnostic claim。\\n\\n\\nMCKP constrained PPL=6.94 vs uniform=7.02，improvement 仅 +1.2%（0.08 PPL gap）。 对比 Qwen7B 的 +27.3%（4.53 PPL gap），14B 的 improvement 在噪声范围内。 原因：14B 有 384 heads，每个 head 承载的 information 更少（head_dim 同为 128，但 48 层分摊）， 2-bit 降级的 per-head cost 更小。MCKP 将 L0 的 4 heads 分配到 8-bit，但这仅节省了 total budget 的很小部分——384 heads 中 4 个 8-bit heads 的 budget 释放被稀释到其余 380 heads， 每个 head 只多获得 ~0.01 bit，不足以改变 bit-width assignment。 Unconstrained ratio=1.44×（类似 Gemma-2 的 1.47×），solver 将 ~80 heads 分配到 2-bit， 产生 moderate 而非 catastrophic degradation。 Decision rule accuracy 从 5/5 降至 5/6：14B 是 false positive（diagnostic 预测 benefit，实际无）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Gemma-2 Constrained MCKP with BOS Fix\",\n    \"description\": \"用 sliding_window + BOS prepend 修正 eval，重测 Gemma-2 constrained MCKP 和 unconstrained baselines。 BOS bug 可能导致之前的 1.47× unconstrained ratio 和 -0.3% constrained delta 不准确。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_baseline_ppl\": 6.03,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 6.17,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_mckp_ppl\": 6.22,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_vs_uniform_pct\": -0.8,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_unconstrained_greedy_ppl\": 7.38,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.22,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_n2bit_unconstrained\": 106,\n      \"gemma2_bos_fix_constrained_bit_dist\": {\n        \"2\": 8,\n        \"4\": 324,\n        \"8\": 4\n      },\n      \"gemma2_old_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.47,\n      \"gemma2_ratio_shift\": -0.25\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Gemma-2 BOS Fix Impact\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"before_bos_fix\",\n          \"after_bos_fix\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline PPL\",\n            \"711.6 (buggy) / 6.03 (corrected)\",\n            6.03,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform 4-bit PPL\",\n            6.17,\n            6.17,\n            \"0.00\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"unconstrained ratio\",\n            \"1.47×\",\n            \"1.22×\",\n            \"-0.25×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"constrained vs uniform\",\n            \"-0.3%\",\n            \"-0.8%\",\n            \"-0.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2-bit heads (unconstrained)\",\n            106,\n            106,\n            \"0\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Revised Three-Tier Labels (COLLAPSED)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"tier\",\n          \"ratio_range\",\n          \"models\",\n          \"count\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Catastrophic\",\n            \"≥2.0×\",\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B (3.31×)\",\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Moderate (EMPTY)\",\n            \"1.25-2.0×\",\n            \"—\",\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mild\",\n            \"1.0-1.25×\",\n            \"Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Gemma-2 1.22×\",\n            4\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三档标签失去 moderate 层：Catastrophic (1 model) + Mild (4 models)， 变成 binary 而非 gradient。原本 \\\"concentration-dependent gradient\\\" 叙事中 Gemma-2 是关键中间证据（flat-high-2bit mechanism），现在该机制的 magnitude  被 BOS bug 虚增。修正后 1.22× 的 over-allocation 仍比 Yi/Llama/Mistral 高， 但 gap 缩小到 0.14-0.15×，可能在 noise 范围内。 论文需要重新校准：要么放弃三档（改用连续变量 regression）， 要么承认 moderate tier 的 evidence 不 robust。\\n\\n\\nBOS fix 降低了 baseline PPL（711.6→6.03 已确认），也降低了 quantized PPL。 关键：BOS bug 对 unconstrained allocation 的影响是 non-uniform 的—— 106 个 2-bit heads 的 joint distortion 在有 BOS token 时部分被 BOS 的 attention mass 吸收 （BOS 通常获得高 attention weight，为后续 token 提供 anchor）， 没有 BOS 时这些 heads 的 distortion 被放大。 修正后 unconstrained ratio 从 1.47× 降至 1.22×，落入 mild 范围（1.07-1.22×）， 与 Yi/Llama/Mistral 的 1.07-1.08× 更接近。 三档标签崩塌：原本 Gemma-2 是 \\\"moderate\\\" 独占，现在没有 moderate 了—— 只有 catastrophic（Qwen7B 3.31×）和 mild（其余 4 个模型 1.07-1.22×）。 Constrained vs uniform 变为 -0.8%（从 -0.3%），方向不变但幅度增大。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0 Auto-Discovery (No L0 Exclusion)\",\n    \"description\": \"去掉 L0 exclusion 硬约束，仅保留 max_2bit=8，观察 solver 是否仍将 L0 heads 分配到 8-bit。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen7b_no_l0excl_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"qwen7b_l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 4,\n      \"qwen7b_solver_auto_discovers_l0\": true,\n      \"qwen14b_no_l0excl_ppl\": 6.97,\n      \"qwen14b_l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 2,\n      \"qwen14b_solver_partial_discovery\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"L0 Auto-Discovery Across Qwen Family\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"l0_dominance\",\n          \"l0_8bit_heads\",\n          \"total_8bit_budget\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"auto_discovery\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            \"26×\",\n            \"4/4\",\n            4,\n            11.23,\n            \"Full ✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            \"8.2×\",\n            \"2/8\",\n            4,\n            6.97,\n            \"Partial ⚠️\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Auto-discovery 在 7B 上完美，在 14B 上部分失败。 Reframed narrative 中这不是 critical：constraint 的价值不依赖 auto-discovery， constraint 的 contribution 是 preventing compounding 而非 discovering structure。\\n\\n\\nQwen7B：solver 从 profiling data 自动将 L0 全部 4 heads 分配到 8-bit（delta 极高，cost-benefit ratio 最优），PPL=11.23 不变。这在 7B 上 works 因为 L0 dominance ratio=26×。 Qwen14B：solver 仅将 L0 的 2/8 heads 分配到 8-bit（L0 dominance ratio 仅 8.2×，不够突出）， 其余 2 个 8-bit 名额给了 L2-L3 的 moderate-delta heads。PPL=6.97（vs constrained 6.94）， 差异很小但说明 14B 的 L0 不再是 unambiguous dominant——auto-discovery 部分失败。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Full Pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B (GQA 4:1) 全 pipeline：profile → constrained MCKP → eval。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_baseline_ppl\": 8.09,\n      \"llama_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n      \"llama_mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n      \"llama_improvement_pct\": 0.2,\n      \"llama_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.07,\n      \"llama_concentration\": 0.57,\n      \"llama_t1_t5\": 0.71,\n      \"llama_shape\": \"Spike (borderline)\",\n      \"llama_natural_k\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"compression\",\n          \"vs_uniform\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline bf16\",\n            8.09,\n            \"1×\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n            8.47,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"constrained MCKP k=8\",\n            8.45,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"+0.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"unconstrained\",\n            8.63,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"-1.9%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 在 worst tier 下保持。但 t₁/t₅=0.71 的 borderline 值  使 diagnostic 对 Llama 的分类依赖 ±0.01 的阈值精度——如果阈值设为 0.75， Llama 会被误分为 Spread，增加 false positive 风险。\\n\\n\\nLlama 的 concentration=0.57 接近 0.50 阈值但 t₁/t₅=0.71 刚好超过 0.70， 被分类为 Spike。实际上 MCKP 仅选择 2 个 heads 做 2-bit（natural k=2）， constraint 从不 bind。+0.2% improvement 在 noise 范围内。 在 worst tier 下，Llama 的 borderline t₁/t₅=0.71 使得 diagnostic boundary  的 robustness 受质疑——0.70 是 arbitrary cutoff。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 Full Pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 全 pipeline，Flat distribution 代表。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mistral_baseline_ppl\": 7.04,\n      \"mistral_uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.13,\n      \"mistral_mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.16,\n      \"mistral_improvement_pct\": -0.4,\n      \"mistral_unconstrained_ratio\": 1.08,\n      \"mistral_concentration\": 0.24,\n      \"mistral_t1_t5\": 0.18,\n      \"mistral_shape\": \"Flat\",\n      \"mistral_k_monotonic\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Mistral-7B Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"compression\",\n          \"vs_uniform\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline bf16\",\n            7.04,\n            \"1×\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n            7.13,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"constrained MCKP k=4\",\n            7.16,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"-0.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"unconstrained\",\n            7.57,\n            \"4×\",\n            \"-6.2%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mistral 是最 clean 的 negative case——profiler signal ≈0， 任何 non-uniform allocation 都 ≤ uniform。在 reframed narrative 中 是 \\\"systematic negative result\\\" 的核心证据之一。\\n\\n\\nMistral concentration=0.24（远低于 0.50），profiler 信号几乎为零。 Constrained MCKP 比 uniform 差 0.4%——solver 分配的 2-bit heads  实际上比 uniform 的 all-4bit 更差。k ablation 单调递增证明  每多一个 2-bit head 都 hurts。在 worst tier 下这是 clean negative， 直接支持 \\\"uniform suffices on flat models\\\" 的叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Compounding Effect Sweep (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 上 sweep max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 PPL vs k curve。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_k0_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"qwen_k4_ppl\": 11.93,\n      \"qwen_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"qwen_k10_ppl\": 11.18,\n      \"qwen_k12_ppl\": 11.21,\n      \"qwen_k16_ppl\": 11.52,\n      \"qwen_k24_ppl\": 13.07,\n      \"qwen_k48_ppl\": 19.84,\n      \"qwen_k75_ppl\": 28.36,\n      \"qwen_k112_ppl\": 36.92,\n      \"elbow_k\": 8,\n      \"curve_shape\": \"U-shape with clear minimum at k≈8-10\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Compounding Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"max_2bit_k\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"delta_vs_k8\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            15.45,\n            \"+37.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            11.93,\n            \"+6.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            11.23,\n            \"baseline (optimal)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            12,\n            11.21,\n            \"-0.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            11.52,\n            \"+2.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            24,\n            13.07,\n            \"+16.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            48,\n            19.84,\n            \"+76.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            112,\n            36.92,\n            \"+228.8%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Compounding curve 是 paper 的 core figure 之一，在 Qwen 上有力。 但在 worst tier 下，其意义从 \\\"universal phenomenon\\\" 缩小为 \\\"Spread-model-specific phenomenon\\\"。Reframe:  compounding 的 magnitude 和 shape 是 architecture-dependent， 但 constraint 在所有模型上都是 safe（≤ uniform）。\\n\\n\\nQwen7B 的 compounding curve 有清晰 U-shape：k 太小（budget 浪费在不需要的 higher-bit heads）， k 太大（compounding 恶化）。Optimal k=8-10 对应 L0 cluster 的 head 数量。 这是 Qwen7B 的固有特性，worst tier 不改变此结果。 但 worst tier 的问题是：此 curve 是否跨模型可复现？ Llama/Mistral 的 k-PPL curve 平坦或单调，没有 U-shape—— compounding 的 \\\"dramatic elbow\\\" 是 Spread-specific，不 universal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (Qwen7B, 2×/4×/8×)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 在三种压缩率下 constrained MCKP vs uniform。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_2x_uniform_ppl\": 10.07,\n      \"qwen_2x_mckp_ppl\": 9.89,\n      \"qwen_2x_improvement_pct\": 1.8,\n      \"qwen_4x_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"qwen_4x_mckp_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"qwen_4x_improvement_pct\": 27.3,\n      \"qwen_8x_uniform_ppl\": 2644.0,\n      \"qwen_8x_mckp_ppl\": 42.6,\n      \"qwen_8x_improvement_pct\": 98.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"compression\",\n          \"uniform_ppl\",\n          \"mckp_ppl\",\n          \"improvement\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"2× (0.50)\",\n            10.07,\n            9.89,\n            \"+1.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4× (0.25)\",\n            15.45,\n            11.23,\n            \"+27.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"8× (0.125)\",\n            2644.0,\n            42.6,\n            \"+98.4%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Budget sweep 在 Qwen 上 compelling。Reframe under worst tier: aggressive compression（5.3×+）即使在 non-Spread 模型上也有 cardinality constraint  的价值（Llama 5.3×: 57.60 vs 2644）——constraint 在极端场景下 universally 有用。\\n\\n\\n2× 压缩：budget 充裕（avg 8-bit），大部分 heads 在安全区，仅 1.8% 改进。 4× 是 sweet spot（27.3%），与已有结果一致。 8× 极端压缩下 uniform = all 2-bit（PPL 2644），constrained MCKP 保护 critical heads 大幅降低 PPL（42.6），但绝对质量仍很差。 Worst tier 不改变 Qwen7B 数字，但 cross-model budget sweep （如果做的话）会显示 Llama/Mistral 在 2× 和 4× 都无 improvement。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"High-Resolution Profiling (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"64 seq × 2048 tokens hires profiling，重跑 MCKP。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hires_constrained_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"lowres_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"hires_improvement_over_lowres_pct\": 2.8,\n      \"hires_nonzero_2bit\": 100,\n      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit\": 37,\n      \"hires_profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Profiling Resolution Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"resolution\",\n          \"nonzero_heads\",\n          \"constrained_ppl\",\n          \"time_min\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"16×512 (lowres)\",\n            37,\n            11.23,\n            \"~10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"64×2048 (hires)\",\n            100,\n            10.91,\n            65.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Hires 提供 modest improvement，但 profiling cost 6× 增加。 在 reframed narrative 中，hires vs lowres 是 secondary concern—— constraint 的 contribution 不依赖 profiling resolution。\\n\\n\\nHires profiling 发现更多 non-zero 2-bit delta heads（100 vs 37）， 改善 MCKP allocation（PPL 10.91 vs 11.23，+2.8%）。 8 个 heads 的 allocation 改变（从 4-bit 到 2-bit 或反向）， 说明 lowres 有 ~7% 的 misallocation。 在 worst tier 下，hires 对 Qwen7B 有 modest benefit， 但对 non-Spread 模型（Llama hires: 8.45 vs 8.50）几乎无差。 且 hires profiling 耗时 65 min（vs lowres ~10 min）， cost/benefit ratio 在非 Spread 模型上 unjustified。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset Evaluation (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"C4 calibration + WikiText-2 evaluation，测试跨 dataset robustness。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_improvement_pct\": 26.9,\n      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"calibration\",\n          \"eval\",\n          \"mckp_ppl\",\n          \"uniform_ppl\",\n          \"improvement\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"WikiText-2\",\n            \"WikiText-2\",\n            11.29,\n            15.45,\n            \"26.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4\",\n            \"WikiText-2\",\n            11.29,\n            15.45,\n            \"26.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WikiText-2\",\n            \"C4\",\n            20.56,\n            35.42,\n            \"42.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-dataset robustness 在 Qwen7B 上 strong（L0 dominance 使得 allocation 稳定）。 但这不 extend 到 non-Spread 模型或 14B（where L0 is less dominant）。\\n\\n\\nAllocation agreement 96.4% 说明 calibration source 对 Qwen7B 影响很小 （112 heads 中仅 4 个 disagree）。这是 因为 L0 的 extreme dominance  在任何 distribution 上都一致——agreement 本质上是 \\\"L0 is always dominant\\\"。 Cross-domain PPL（20.56）比 same-domain（11.29）高很多， 但 vs uniform 仍有大幅改善（20.56 vs 35.42）。 Worst tier 的问题：14B 上 agreement 可能更低（L0 dominance 弱， mid-layer allocation 更 distribution-dependent）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy (Algorithm 1) on {2,4,8,16} vs constrained MCKP。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n      \"greedy_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"greedy_constrained_delta_vs_mckp\": 0.0012,\n      \"bit_distribution\": {\n        \"2\": 8,\n        \"4\": 100,\n        \"8\": 4\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Solver Comparison (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"unconstrained_ppl\",\n          \"constrained_k8_ppl\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RateQuant Greedy\",\n            32.45,\n            11.23\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP\",\n            36.92,\n            11.23\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"—\",\n            15.45\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Solver equivalence under constraint 是 robust result，在 worst tier 下 成为 paper 的 core contribution 之一（不依赖 diagnostic）。\\n\\n\\nUnconstrained greedy (32.45) 和 MCKP (36.92) 都 catastrophically fail。 Constrained 后两者 converge（Δ=0.0012 ≈ 0）。 这是 \\\"constraint is the contribution, not the solver\\\" 的 strongest evidence。 Worst tier 不改变此结论——solver equivalence under constraint  是 Qwen7B 的数学属性（constrained feasible set small enough）， 无论 diagnostic 是否成立。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Oracle Comparison (Brute-Force Subset)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen7B 3-4 layer groups 上 brute-force optimal vs MCKP。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0183,\n      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0046,\n      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n      \"gap_nature\": \"2-bit head position swap within same bit budget\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Oracle vs MCKP (Qwen2.5-7B Subset)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer_group\",\n          \"mckp_ppl\",\n          \"oracle_ppl\",\n          \"gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"L0-L3\",\n            10.91,\n            10.91,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"L1\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.0183\n          ],\n          [\n            \"L4\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.0045\n          ],\n          [\n            \"L11\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.0136\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Near-optimality 是 standalone result，加强 constraint contribution。\\n\\n\\nMCKP gap to oracle 极小（max 0.0183 PPL），5/8 layers 完全 optimal。 Gap 来源：3 个 layer 上 MCKP 选了 slightly suboptimal 的 2-bit head 位置， 但 bit budget 完全相同——差异仅在 which head gets 2-bit，非结构性错误。 即使在 worst tier 下，MCKP near-optimality 成立——这不依赖 diagnostic。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Domain Calibration Robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"C4 calibrate / WikiText-2 evaluate 及反向，报告 allocation agreement。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_agreement\": 0.964,\n      \"llama_agreement\": 0.977,\n      \"mistral_agreement\": 0.965,\n      \"qwen14b_predicted_agreement\": 0.88\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Calibration Agreement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"agreement\",\n          \"heads_agree\",\n          \"total\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            \"96.4%\",\n            108,\n            112\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            \"97.7%\",\n            250,\n            256\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            \"96.5%\",\n            247,\n            256\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B (predicted)\",\n            \"~88%\",\n            \"~338\",\n            384\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-calibration robustness 在小模型上 strong， 但可能不 scale to larger models（more heads → more ambiguity）。\\n\\n\\n三个 7-9B 模型都有 >96% agreement，说明 calibration robust。 但 worst tier 预测 Qwen14B 的 agreement 可能降至 ~88%， 因为 14B 的 sensitivity 更分散、mid-layer heads 的 ranking  更 distribution-dependent。这削弱 \\\"one-shot calibration\\\" 的 practicality claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Head Sensitivity Visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper-quality figures: per-head delta heatmap, compounding curve, allocation comparison。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"figures_generated\": 5,\n      \"key_visual\": \"5-model heatmap comparison shows architecture diversity\",\n      \"worst_tier_impact\": \"14B heatmap looks like diluted version of 7B, weakens family consistency\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Visualization 诚实展示 diagnostic 的 limitation 反而增加 credibility。 14B false positive 在 scatter plot 上是 visible anomaly，需要 explicit 讨论。\\n\\n\\nVisualization 不产生新数据但在 worst tier 下需要更新： (1) 加入 14B heatmap 显示 diluted spread pattern（与 7B 对比削弱 Qwen family story） (2) 三档 gradient bar chart 中 moderate 消失（Gemma-2 BOS fix） (3) Decision rule scatter 中 14B 落在 Spread 象限但标记为 false positive\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Downstream Task Evaluation (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"ARC-C / HellaSwag / PIQA / WinoGrande on Qwen7B + 4 non-Spread models at 4×。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n      \"qwen_arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n      \"yi_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.77,\n      \"llama_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.99,\n      \"mistral_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.48,\n      \"gemma2_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": 0.14,\n      \"qwen14b_predicted_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": -0.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Downstream Summary (6 Models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"shape\",\n          \"mckp_vs_uniform_pp\",\n          \"diagnostic_correct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            \"Spread\",\n            \"+2.60pp\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            \"Diluted Spread\",\n            \"-0.2pp (noise)\",\n            \"❌ FP\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi-1.5-9B\",\n            \"Spike\",\n            \"-0.77pp\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            \"Spike\",\n            \"-0.99pp\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            \"Flat\",\n            \"-0.48pp\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n            \"Flat\",\n            \"+0.14pp (noise)\",\n            \"✅\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Downstream data 在 worst tier 下 reinforces \\\"1/6 models benefit\\\"—— 更适合 framing 为 systematic negative result + one strong positive case study。\\n\\n\\n5-model downstream data 完整，结果与 PPL 一致。 Worst tier 预测 Qwen14B downstream：MCKP vs uniform ≈ -0.2pp（与 PPL 的 +1.2% 不一致方向？ 不，PPL improvement +1.2% 意味着 MCKP 稍好，downstream 可能 +0.1-0.3pp 或 noise）。 但 14B 的 downstream 数据不足以区分 signal vs noise（无 multi-seed CI）。 论文需报告 14B 但不能 claim benefit。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"70B Profiling-Only (Qwen2.5-72B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B distortion profiling（不做 eval），分析 sensitivity 是否随 model size 缩放。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen72b_concentration\": 0.48,\n      \"qwen72b_t1_t5\": 0.69,\n      \"qwen72b_l0_dominance_ratio\": 5.1,\n      \"qwen72b_total_heads\": 640,\n      \"qwen72b_diagnostic_prediction\": \"borderline (conc<0.50)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Qwen Family Scaling\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"params\",\n          \"layers\",\n          \"kv_heads\",\n          \"concentration\",\n          \"t1_t5\",\n          \"predicted_shape\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            \"7B\",\n            28,\n            112,\n            0.61,\n            0.57,\n            \"Spread\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            \"14B\",\n            48,\n            384,\n            0.55,\n            0.63,\n            \"Diluted Spread\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-72B\",\n            \"72B\",\n            80,\n            640,\n            0.48,\n            0.69,\n            \"Borderline/Flat\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"如果 72B profiling 证实 concentration < 0.50，则 Spread pattern  不是 Qwen architecture 的固有属性而是 small-model artifact。 这对 diagnostic 的 practical value 是致命打击—— practitioner 最关心的 large models 恰恰最不可能是 Spread。\\n\\n\\n72B 有 80 layers × 8 KV heads = 640 heads。更多层进一步稀释 concentration。 Concentration=0.48（刚低于 0.50 阈值），t₁/t₅=0.69（刚低于 0.70）。 Diagnostic 预测 borderline/Flat——如果确实如此， 则 Qwen 模型族呈现 \\\"7B=Spread, 14B=Diluted Spread, 72B=Flat\\\" 的递减梯度， 说明 model size increase 系统性地 dilute sensitivity concentration。 这直接挑战 \\\"Qwen family is Spread\\\" 的 assumption。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"K/V Separation\",\n    \"description\": \"将 K 和 V heads 作为独立 MCKP items，允许 asymmetric K/V budget。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.31,\n      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"K/V Separation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"ppl\",\n          \"k_2bit\",\n          \"v_2bit\",\n          \"vs_joint\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Joint K+V\",\n            10.91,\n            4,\n            4,\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K/V separated\",\n            11.22,\n            16,\n            0,\n            \"+2.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            0,\n            0,\n            \"+41.6%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative result：K/V separation 不如 joint optimization。 论文用 1 paragraph 报告，作为 RateQuant comparison 的补充。\\n\\n\\nK/V separation 让 solver 独立优化 K 和 V 的 budget。 结果：V heads 全部 4-bit（sensitivity 低），K heads 有 16 个 2-bit（budget 被 V 让渡）。 但 PPL 11.22 略差于 joint optimization 的 10.91（Δ=0.31）， 因为 K-only 2-bit 的 compounding 比 joint 分配更 aggressive。 在 worst tier 下，这是 negative result——joint optimization 优于 separation， 说明 K/V interaction matters，简单的 asymmetric budget 不够。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0-Only Heuristic Baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"最简单的 non-uniform 策略：L0 全部 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit。 如果匹配 MCKP，则 full optimization 不必要。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_l0_random_mean\": 11.69,\n      \"qwen_l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n      \"qwen_l0_random_std\": 0.47,\n      \"qwen_naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n      \"qwen_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"llama_l0_random_mean\": 10.48,\n      \"llama_mckp_ppl\": 8.45,\n      \"mistral_l0_random_mean\": 7.56,\n      \"mistral_mckp_ppl\": 7.16\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"L0 Heuristic vs MCKP\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"l0_random_median\",\n          \"mckp\",\n          \"uniform\",\n          \"mckp_vs_heuristic_gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            11.52,\n            10.91,\n            15.45,\n            \"5.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            10.04,\n            8.45,\n            8.47,\n            \"18.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            7.59,\n            7.16,\n            7.13,\n            \"6.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MCKP outperforms heuristic on all models，但 gap varies。 在 non-Spread models，MCKP 和 heuristic 都 ≤ uniform—— the right choice is \\\"don't bother\\\" rather than \\\"optimize better\\\"。\\n\\n\\nL0-random heuristic（随机选 k 个 non-L0 heads 做 2-bit）在 Qwen 上 median=11.52 vs MCKP=10.91（gap 5.6%）。MCKP 的优势来自  precisely 选择 which non-L0 heads 做 2-bit（vs random）。 在 Llama/Mistral 上 L0-random 显著差于 MCKP（且 MCKP ≈ uniform）， 说明 heuristic 不是 universal substitute。 Worst tier 的 concern：14B 上 L0-random 可能 ≈ MCKP（因为 14B 的 MCKP 本身 ≈ uniform）， 进一步削弱 MCKP 的 value proposition。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy + Cardinality Constraint\",\n    \"description\": \"验证 constraint 是否是 key contribution（vs solver choice）。 Greedy + k=8 vs MCKP + k=8 vs both unconstrained。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n      \"greedy_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"mckp_constrained_k8_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"delta_greedy_vs_mckp_constrained\": 0.0012,\n      \"solver_equivalence\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Solver Equivalence Under Constraint\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"unconstrained\",\n          \"constrained_k8\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RateQuant Greedy\",\n            32.45,\n            11.23,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP\",\n            36.92,\n            11.23,\n            \"Δ=0.0012\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 reframed worst-tier narrative 中，solver equivalence under constraint  成为 Claim 1 的 core evidence。不需要 diagnostic 来 motivate。\\n\\n\\nCore finding：constraint 使 greedy = MCKP（Δ=0.0012 ≈ 0）。 Constrained feasible set 小到 greedy 的 local search 等于 global optimum。 这是 paper 最 robust 的 result——不依赖 diagnostic，不依赖 model choice， 纯数学属性。在 worst tier 下这是 anchor result。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Error Bars (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"3 个 calibration seed 的 constrained MCKP，报告 mean±std。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_seed0\": 11.02,\n      \"mckp_seed1\": 10.9,\n      \"mckp_seed2\": 11.05,\n      \"mckp_mean\": 10.99,\n      \"mckp_std\": 0.065,\n      \"uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n      \"bit_dist_all_seeds\": \"2:8, 4:100, 8:4\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Results (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"mckp_ppl\",\n          \"bit_dist\",\n          \"agreement_with_seed0\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"seed_0\",\n            11.02,\n            \"8:100:4\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_1\",\n            10.9,\n            \"8:100:4\",\n            \"94.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_2\",\n            11.05,\n            \"8:100:4\",\n            \"91.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean±std\",\n            \"10.99±0.065\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Qwen7B 的 statistical robustness 是 solid。但 N=3 seeds 仍然 limited。 论文应报告 \\\"our main result is robust to calibration variation\\\" 但  not claim \\\"statistical significance\\\" formally。\\n\\n\\n三个 seed 的 MCKP PPL std=0.065（mean=10.99），95% CI = [10.86, 11.12]。 与 uniform 的 gap（15.45 - 10.99 = 4.46）远大于 CI width（0.26）， Qwen7B 上的 improvement 是 statistically robust。 Bit distribution 三个 seed 完全一致（8:100:4），allocation agreement 90.2% （head-level 有 10% variation 但 bit-level distribution 不变）。 Worst tier 的 concern：14B 上 std 可能更大（sensitivity 更分散 → calibration noise 更大）， 且 improvement 本身在 noise 范围内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Runtime/Latency Benchmark (Qwen7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"端到端 inference latency 和 throughput。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bf16_prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n      \"uniform4_prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n      \"uniform4_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n      \"mckp_prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n      \"mckp_throughput_tok_s\": 21.8,\n      \"uniform4_throughput_tok_s\": 23.6,\n      \"mckp_solver_sec\": 0.005,\n      \"mckp_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 8.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Runtime Benchmark (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"prefill_ms\",\n          \"decode_ms\",\n          \"throughput\",\n          \"memory_MB\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"bf16\",\n            45.86,\n            33.78,\n            \"29.6 tok/s\",\n            21.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform 4-bit\",\n            54.25,\n            42.46,\n            \"23.6 tok/s\",\n            5.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP constrained\",\n            57.03,\n            46.09,\n            \"21.8 tok/s\",\n            5.25\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"8.5% latency overhead 是 acceptable trade-off 但仅在 Spread models 上。 Reframe: \\\"if diagnostic uncertain, use uniform 4-bit to avoid latency cost\\\"  — 这与 worst-tier narrative 的 \\\"conservative recommendation\\\" 一致。\\n\\n\\nMixed-precision MCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 慢 ~8.5%（decode 46.09 vs 42.46 ms/tok）， 因为 mixed bit-width 需要 per-head dequantize dispatch（vs uniform 的 vectorized batch dequant）。 内存相同（5.25 MB），solver 本身 negligible（5ms）。 Worst tier 的 concern：8.5% latency overhead 换 PPL improvement 仅在 Qwen7B 上 worth it—— 在 non-Spread 模型上 overhead 仍存在但 PPL 无 improvement， 纯亏损。Reviewer 会问 \\\"when is the latency cost justified?\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"W9 Compounding Scaling (Worst Tier)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen7B 上 top-k vs random-k 2-bit assignment sweep，刻画 super-additivity。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k1_topk_ppl\": 9.83,\n      \"k1_randomk_ppl\": 9.89,\n      \"k4_topk_ppl\": 9.85,\n      \"k4_randomk_ppl\": 10.06,\n      \"k8_topk_ppl\": 10.04,\n      \"k8_randomk_ppl\": 11.07,\n      \"k16_topk_ppl\": 10.42,\n      \"k16_randomk_ppl\": 12.91,\n      \"k32_topk_ppl\": 11.6,\n      \"k32_randomk_ppl\": 18.33,\n      \"k64_topk_ppl\": 22.95,\n      \"k64_randomk_ppl\": 55.94,\n      \"k64_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.45,\n      \"k32_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.58,\n      \"k16_randomk_topk_ratio\": 1.24,\n      \"non_monotonic_flag\": true,\n      \"variance_at_k16_masks_trend\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"W9 Compounding (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"k\",\n          \"topk_ppl\",\n          \"randomk_ppl\",\n          \"randomk_std\",\n          \"ratio\",\n          \"monotonic\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            9.83,\n            9.89,\n            0.05,\n            1.0,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            9.85,\n            10.06,\n            0.06,\n            1.24,\n            \"↑\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            10.04,\n            11.07,\n            0.69,\n            1.76,\n            \"↑\"\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            10.42,\n            12.91,\n            0.4,\n            1.24,\n            \"↓ ⚠️\"\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            11.6,\n            18.33,\n            2.53,\n            1.58,\n            \"↑\"\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            22.95,\n            55.94,\n            9.73,\n            1.45,\n            \"↓ ⚠️\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 worst tier 下，W9 data 的 non-monotonicity 和 high variance  使得 formal super-additivity claim 不成立。 Reframe: 报告为 \\\"empirical observation of compounding trend with substantial variance\\\"， 不 formalize 为 theorem 或 proposition。 Compounding 的 qualitative story 仍 hold（ratio >1 at all k>1）， 但 quantitative precision 不足以支撑 formal contribution。\\n\\n\\nWorst-tier 下 k=64 的 randomk/topk ratio 降至 1.45（vs 实际 2.44 的 actual data 中位估计）。 k=8-16 区间出现 non-monotonic：k=8 ratio=1.76 但 k=16 ratio 回落到 1.24， 然后 k=32 又升到 1.58。这种 non-monotonicity 可能来自： (1) random-k 的 seed variance（std=0.4-2.5 across seeds）， (2) top-k 在某些 k 值恰好避开 interaction cluster 而 random 没有。 Non-monotonic behavior 使得 \\\"super-additivity monotonically increases with k\\\"  的 clean story 不成立。论文需要 acknowledge variance 并报告 CI。 ratio 的 overall trend 仍是 increasing（1.24→1.45→1.58→1.45）， 但 non-monotonicity at intermediate k 削弱 formalization strength。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen2.5-14B Downstream Eval (Predicted)\",\n    \"description\": \"如果 14B profiling + MCKP 完成，需跑 downstream eval 验证 PPL 与 downstream 一致性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen14b_baseline_avg\": 0.72,\n      \"qwen14b_uniform_avg\": 0.71,\n      \"qwen14b_mckp_avg\": 0.71,\n      \"qwen14b_mckp_vs_uniform_pp\": 0.1,\n      \"qwen14b_arc_challenge_delta_pp\": -0.5,\n      \"qwen14b_hellaswag_delta_pp\": 0.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Qwen14B Downstream (Predicted)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task\",\n          \"uniform\",\n          \"mckp\",\n          \"delta_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"arc_challenge\",\n            0.58,\n            0.575,\n            \"-0.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"hellaswag\",\n            0.72,\n            0.723,\n            \"+0.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"piqa\",\n            0.81,\n            0.811,\n            \"+0.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"winogrande\",\n            0.73,\n            0.728,\n            \"-0.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"average\",\n            0.71,\n            0.71,\n            \"+0.1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Downstream 确认 14B false positive——不仅 PPL 无 improvement， downstream 也在 noise。论文需要 transparent reporting。\\n\\nPPL improvement +1.2% → downstream ≈ 0pp（noise）。 arc_challenge 可能略负（-0.5pp），与跨模型的 arc_challenge 系统性敏感一致。 hellaswag 略正（+0.3pp）但在 seed noise 范围内。 整体结论：14B downstream 与 PPL 一致——MCKP 无 meaningful benefit。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1313,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1313}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnvGvhzwTCHdooGEQt252p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ratekv\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n6\t- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n7\t\n8\t## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n9\t\n10\t**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n11\t\n12\t**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n13\t\n14\t| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n15\t|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n16\t| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n17\t| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n18\t| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n19\t| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n20\t\n21\t## Core Insight\n22\t\n23\tPer-head KV cache quantization sensitivity varies dramatically across architectures, and the effectiveness of non-uniform mixed-precision allocation is fundamentally determined by the degree of this heterogeneity. We provide both the analysis framework — characterizing when non-uniform quantization helps via per-head sensitivity concentration metrics — and a surprisingly simple method fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding effects from profiler non-additivity and reduces the search space sufficiently that solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy and MCKP produce identical allocations).\n24\t\n25\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n26\t\n27\t1. **Head sensitivity heterogeneity is architecture-dependent and determined by sensitivity *distribution shape*, not GQA ratio or concentration alone**: Per-KV-head quantization sensitivity is extremely non-uniform within models, but whether MCKP can exploit this heterogeneity depends on the *shape* of the sensitivity distribution, not just its magnitude. Critical counterexample: Yi-1.5-9B (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — the *highest* in our lineup) provides *no benefit* from MCKP (7.22 vs 7.22 uniform), while Qwen2.5-7B (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61) succeeds (+27.3%). The difference is distribution shape: Qwen has a *cluster* of sensitive heads (Layer 0, 4 heads with cross-bitwidth gradients — \"spread\" pattern, t₁/t₅=0.57), while Yi-1.5 has a single extreme outlier (L4H3, delta=13.12, t₁/t₅=0.90 — \"spike\" pattern) with sensitivity at only one bitwidth. A joint diagnostic — concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 — correctly separates the beneficial case (Qwen) from all four non-beneficial cases across five architectures. Three shape categories emerge:\n28\t   - **Spread** (Qwen): high concentration + low t₁/t₅ → multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients → MCKP effective\n29\t   - **Spike** (Yi-1.5, Llama): high t₁/t₅ → single outlier dominates → MCKP ineffective\n30\t   - **Flat** (Mistral, Gemma-2): low concentration → near-uniform sensitivity → MCKP ineffective (t₁/t₅ irrelevant when concentration < 0.50)\n31\t\n32\t2. **Cardinality constraint is the primary intervention; unconstrained catastrophe is Spread-specific**: On non-consecutive discrete bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, unconstrained allocation produces **catastrophic** results on Spread-heterogeneity architectures (Qwen: greedy 32.45, MCKP 36.92 vs uniform 15.45 = 3.31× baseline) because per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when many heads are simultaneously assigned extreme quantization. On non-Spread architectures, unconstrained allocation causes **mild-to-moderate degradation** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Gemma-2 1.47×) but still underperforms uniform 4-bit in all cases — the solver over-allocates 2-bit heads even when individual distortions appear small. A cardinality constraint (max_2bit≤k) is a simple and sufficient condition: it prevents compounding on Spread models, avoids 2-bit over-allocation on non-Spread models, AND reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce identical bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000, both 11.2312). **Practical implication**: the concentration diagnostic determines whether to invest in MCKP + constraint (Spread models) or simply use uniform 4-bit (non-Spread models — saves solver computation with no quality loss). The profiling benefit beyond the constraint (hires vs lowres) is architecture-dependent: substantial on Spread models (Qwen), marginal on others. The optimal k is determinable via small-scale compounding effect test (plan_004).\n33\t\n34\t**Claim 2 three-pillar support** (Reviewer Q4, new narrative STRENGTHENS Claim 2):\n35\t1. Spread models: constraint prevents catastrophe (Qwen 32.45→11.23)\n36\t2. Flat models: constraint prevents moderate over-allocation (Gemma-2 8.85→~6.17, 106→8 heads at 2-bit)\n37\t3. All models: constraint makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000)\n38\tThis answers \"when\" and \"why\", not just \"what\" — stronger than original \"universal catastrophe\" narrative.\n39\t\n40\t3. **A joint empirical decision rule correctly separates beneficial from non-beneficial architectures**: Constrained allocation achieves 27.3% PPL improvement on Qwen (spread pattern: concentration 0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57), while providing no benefit on Yi-1.5 (spike: 0.71, t₁/t₅=0.90, ≈0%), Llama (spike: 0.34, t₁/t₅=0.71, +0.2%), Mistral (flat: 0.22, t₁/t₅=0.18, -0.4%), and Gemma-2 (flat: 0.23, t₁/t₅=0.38, -0.3%). The joint condition — concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 — correctly separates the beneficial case from all four non-beneficial cases across five architectures (5/5 accuracy). Concentration alone fails: Yi-1.5 (0.71) exceeds Qwen (0.61) yet gains nothing, because its spike pattern (single outlier, no cross-bitwidth gradient) cannot be exploited. Under aggressive compression (≥5×), constrained allocation prevents catastrophic collapse even on non-beneficial architectures (Llama 5.3×: constrained PPL 57.60 vs uniform 2-bit 2644). This provides practitioners an empirical decision rule for when to invest in mixed-precision KV cache quantization. **Claim strength note (Reviewer-verified)**: N=1 Spread → position as \"empirical decision rule\", NOT \"diagnostic framework\". If Qwen2.5-14B also confirms Spread → upgrade to \"empirical diagnostic\" (N=2).\n41\t\n42\t## Story Spine\n43\t\n44\t- **Problem**: KV cache quantization typically applies uniform bit-width across all heads. Per-head mixed-precision allocation promises better quality-compression tradeoffs, but two fundamental questions remain unanswered: (1) *when* does non-uniform allocation actually help — i.e., under what architectural and compression conditions does the added complexity pay off? (2) *how* to make existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) work correctly on hardware-aligned discrete bit-widths {2,4,8,16} where they currently fail catastrophically?\n45\t\n46\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant (May 2026) provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form (Theorem 2) and discrete greedy (Algorithm 1, optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6} per Proposition 6). However, on hardware-aligned non-consecutive sets {2,4,8,16}, RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 (vs optimal ~11.23) — the polymatroid structure that guarantees greedy optimality breaks. Moreover, unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding effects from profiler non-additivity. Critically, neither RateQuant nor ARKV addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is beneficial.\n47\t\n48\t- **Our framing**: We present a systematic study of per-head KV cache quantization sensitivity across architectures and identify a surprisingly simple fix for the failure of existing algorithms on hardware-aligned bit-widths: a cardinality constraint limiting the number of heads assigned to extreme quantization levels. This single intervention (a) prevents compounding effects, (b) reduces the search space to where solver choice is irrelevant — greedy and MCKP produce identical optimal allocations, and (c) can be parameterized via a small-scale compounding test. Beyond the method, we establish that the benefit of non-uniform allocation is architecture-dependent and quantifiable via an empirical decision rule (concentration + distribution shape), providing practitioners a two-metric check for when mixed-precision is worthwhile.\n49\t\n50\t- **Headline result template**: \"We show that the benefit of non-uniform per-head KV cache quantization is concentration-dependent: on spread-heterogeneity architectures (Qwen, concentration 0.61), unconstrained solvers fail catastrophically (PPL 32-37 vs uniform 15.45), while a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) achieves 27.3% PPL improvement with identical results from greedy and MCKP (Δ=0.0000). On non-spread architectures (4 models, 1.07-1.47× baseline), unconstrained solvers cause only mild degradation, and constrained MCKP offers no benefit over uniform 4-bit at either PPL or downstream task level (<1pp avg). An empirical decision rule (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly separates the beneficial case from all four non-beneficial cases (5/5 accuracy) at both PPL and downstream task level, providing practitioners a two-metric check to determine whether mixed-precision KV cache quantization is worthwhile — or whether uniform quantization suffices.\"\n51\t\n52\t## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n53\t\n54\tFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n55\t\n56\t| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n57\t|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n58\t| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n59\t| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 34% of total delta) |\n60\t| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.34-0.59 | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n61\t| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n62\t| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n63\t\n64\t**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n65\t\n66\t**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n67\t\n68\t**Joint diagnostic** (n=5, 5/5 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike) and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n69\t\n70\t## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n71\t\n72\t| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n73\t|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n74\t| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n75\t| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n76\t| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n77\t| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n78\t| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n79\t\n80\tKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n81\t\n82\t## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n83\t\n84\t| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n85\t|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n86\t| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n87\t| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n88\t| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | 0.57 (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (borderline t₁/t₅=0.71) | ≈ Marginal |\n89\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n90\t| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n91\t\n92\t**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n93\t- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n94\t- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n95\t- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n96\t- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n97\t\n98\t**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n99\t\n100\tThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n101\t- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n102\t- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n103\t- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n104\t\n105\tReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n106\t\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n107\t\n108\tThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n109\t\n110\t⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n111\t\n112\t**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n113\t\n114\t**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n115\t\n116\t### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n117\t\n118\tPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n119\t\n120\t| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n121\t|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n122\t| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n123\t| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n124\t| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n125\t| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n126\t| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n127\t| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n128\t\n129\tContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n130\t\n131\t### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n132\t\n133\tAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n134\t\n135\t### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n136\t\n137\t**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n138\t\n139\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n140\t|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n141\t| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n142\t| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n143\t| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n144\t| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n145\t| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n146\t\n147\t**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n148\t\n149\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n150\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n151\t| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n152\t| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n153\t| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n154\t| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n155\t| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n156\t| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n157\t\n158\t**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n159\t\n160\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n161\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n162\t| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n163\t| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n164\t| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n165\t| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n166\t| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n167\t| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n168\t\n169\t**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n170\t\n171\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n172\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n173\t| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n174\t| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n175\t| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n176\t| piqa | — | — | — |\n177\t| winogrande | — | — | — |\n178\t| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n179\t\n180\t**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n181\t\n182\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n183\t|------|---------------|------|---|\n184\t| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n185\t\n186\t**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n187\t- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n188\t- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n189\t- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n190\t- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n191\t- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n192\t- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n193\t- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n194\t- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n195\t- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n196\t\n197\t## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n198\t\n199\tAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n200\t\n201\t| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n202\t|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n203\t| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n204\t| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n205\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n206\t\n207\t**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n208\t\n209\t**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n210\t\n211\t## Differentiation from RateQuant\n212\t\n213\t| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n214\t|--------|-----------|------|\n215\t| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n216\t| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n217\t| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n218\t| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n219\t| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n220\t| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n221\t| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n222\t\n223\t## Venue Fit Risks\n224\t\n225\t- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n226\t- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n227\t- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n228\t- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 5/5 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n229\t- **Statistical power**: n=5 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 5 architectures\" or \"5/5 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n230\t- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n231\t\n232\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n233\t\n234\t1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n235\t2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n236\t3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n237\t4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n238\t5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n239\t6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n240\t7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n241\t8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n242\t9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n243\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60b94339-87f0-47ef-aa74-b7c45d2f68d8","uuid":"5bbd3489-c8ec-45e1-b2d2-e21ba2cf2e4e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:54:32.491Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T085855/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ratekv\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n\n## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n\n**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n\n**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n\n| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n\n## Core Insight\n\nPer-head KV cache quantization sensitivity varies dramatically across architectures, and the effectiveness of non-uniform mixed-precision allocation is fundamentally determined by the degree of this heterogeneity. We provide both the analysis framework — characterizing when non-uniform quantization helps via per-head sensitivity concentration metrics — and a surprisingly simple method fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding effects from profiler non-additivity and reduces the search space sufficiently that solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy and MCKP produce identical allocations).\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Head sensitivity heterogeneity is architecture-dependent and determined by sensitivity *distribution shape*, not GQA ratio or concentration alone**: Per-KV-head quantization sensitivity is extremely non-uniform within models, but whether MCKP can exploit this heterogeneity depends on the *shape* of the sensitivity distribution, not just its magnitude. Critical counterexample: Yi-1.5-9B (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — the *highest* in our lineup) provides *no benefit* from MCKP (7.22 vs 7.22 uniform), while Qwen2.5-7B (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61) succeeds (+27.3%). The difference is distribution shape: Qwen has a *cluster* of sensitive heads (Layer 0, 4 heads with cross-bitwidth gradients — \"spread\" pattern, t₁/t₅=0.57), while Yi-1.5 has a single extreme outlier (L4H3, delta=13.12, t₁/t₅=0.90 — \"spike\" pattern) with sensitivity at only one bitwidth. A joint diagnostic — concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 — correctly separates the beneficial case (Qwen) from all four non-beneficial cases across five architectures. Three shape categories emerge:\n   - **Spread** (Qwen): high concentration + low t₁/t₅ → multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients → MCKP effective\n   - **Spike** (Yi-1.5, Llama): high t₁/t₅ → single outlier dominates → MCKP ineffective\n   - **Flat** (Mistral, Gemma-2): low concentration → near-uniform sensitivity → MCKP ineffective (t₁/t₅ irrelevant when concentration < 0.50)\n\n2. **Cardinality constraint is the primary intervention; unconstrained catastrophe is Spread-specific**: On non-consecutive discrete bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, unconstrained allocation produces **catastrophic** results on Spread-heterogeneity architectures (Qwen: greedy 32.45, MCKP 36.92 vs uniform 15.45 = 3.31× baseline) because per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when many heads are simultaneously assigned extreme quantization. On non-Spread architectures, unconstrained allocation causes **mild-to-moderate degradation** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Gemma-2 1.47×) but still underperforms uniform 4-bit in all cases — the solver over-allocates 2-bit heads even when individual distortions appear small. A cardinality constraint (max_2bit≤k) is a simple and sufficient condition: it prevents compounding on Spread models, avoids 2-bit over-allocation on non-Spread models, AND reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce identical bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000, both 11.2312). **Practical implication**: the concentration diagnostic determines whether to invest in MCKP + constraint (Spread models) or simply use uniform 4-bit (non-Spread models — saves solver computation with no quality loss). The profiling benefit beyond the constraint (hires vs lowres) is architecture-dependent: substantial on Spread models (Qwen), marginal on others. The optimal k is determinable via small-scale compounding effect test (plan_004).\n\n**Claim 2 three-pillar support** (Reviewer Q4, new narrative STRENGTHENS Claim 2):\n1. Spread models: constraint prevents catastrophe (Qwen 32.45→11.23)\n2. Flat models: constraint prevents moderate over-allocation (Gemma-2 8.85→~6.17, 106→8 heads at 2-bit)\n3. All models: constraint makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000)\nThis answers \"when\" and \"why\", not just \"what\" — stronger than original \"universal catastrophe\" narrative.\n\n3. **A joint empirical decision rule correctly separates beneficial from non-beneficial architectures**: Constrained allocation achieves 27.3% PPL improvement on Qwen (spread pattern: concentration 0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57), while providing no benefit on Yi-1.5 (spike: 0.71, t₁/t₅=0.90, ≈0%), Llama (spike: 0.34, t₁/t₅=0.71, +0.2%), Mistral (flat: 0.22, t₁/t₅=0.18, -0.4%), and Gemma-2 (flat: 0.23, t₁/t₅=0.38, -0.3%). The joint condition — concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 — correctly separates the beneficial case from all four non-beneficial cases across five architectures (5/5 accuracy). Concentration alone fails: Yi-1.5 (0.71) exceeds Qwen (0.61) yet gains nothing, because its spike pattern (single outlier, no cross-bitwidth gradient) cannot be exploited. Under aggressive compression (≥5×), constrained allocation prevents catastrophic collapse even on non-beneficial architectures (Llama 5.3×: constrained PPL 57.60 vs uniform 2-bit 2644). This provides practitioners an empirical decision rule for when to invest in mixed-precision KV cache quantization. **Claim strength note (Reviewer-verified)**: N=1 Spread → position as \"empirical decision rule\", NOT \"diagnostic framework\". If Qwen2.5-14B also confirms Spread → upgrade to \"empirical diagnostic\" (N=2).\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: KV cache quantization typically applies uniform bit-width across all heads. Per-head mixed-precision allocation promises better quality-compression tradeoffs, but two fundamental questions remain unanswered: (1) *when* does non-uniform allocation actually help — i.e., under what architectural and compression conditions does the added complexity pay off? (2) *how* to make existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) work correctly on hardware-aligned discrete bit-widths {2,4,8,16} where they currently fail catastrophically?\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant (May 2026) provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form (Theorem 2) and discrete greedy (Algorithm 1, optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6} per Proposition 6). However, on hardware-aligned non-consecutive sets {2,4,8,16}, RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 (vs optimal ~11.23) — the polymatroid structure that guarantees greedy optimality breaks. Moreover, unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding effects from profiler non-additivity. Critically, neither RateQuant nor ARKV addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is beneficial.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present a systematic study of per-head KV cache quantization sensitivity across architectures and identify a surprisingly simple fix for the failure of existing algorithms on hardware-aligned bit-widths: a cardinality constraint limiting the number of heads assigned to extreme quantization levels. This single intervention (a) prevents compounding effects, (b) reduces the search space to where solver choice is irrelevant — greedy and MCKP produce identical optimal allocations, and (c) can be parameterized via a small-scale compounding test. Beyond the method, we establish that the benefit of non-uniform allocation is architecture-dependent and quantifiable via an empirical decision rule (concentration + distribution shape), providing practitioners a two-metric check for when mixed-precision is worthwhile.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"We show that the benefit of non-uniform per-head KV cache quantization is concentration-dependent: on spread-heterogeneity architectures (Qwen, concentration 0.61), unconstrained solvers fail catastrophically (PPL 32-37 vs uniform 15.45), while a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) achieves 27.3% PPL improvement with identical results from greedy and MCKP (Δ=0.0000). On non-spread architectures (4 models, 1.07-1.47× baseline), unconstrained solvers cause only mild degradation, and constrained MCKP offers no benefit over uniform 4-bit at either PPL or downstream task level (<1pp avg). An empirical decision rule (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly separates the beneficial case from all four non-beneficial cases (5/5 accuracy) at both PPL and downstream task level, providing practitioners a two-metric check to determine whether mixed-precision KV cache quantization is worthwhile — or whether uniform quantization suffices.\"\n\n## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n\nFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n\n| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 34% of total delta) |\n| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.34-0.59 | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n\n**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n\n**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n\n**Joint diagnostic** (n=5, 5/5 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike) and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n\n## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n\n| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n\nKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n\n## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n\n| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | 0.57 (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (borderline t₁/t₅=0.71) | ≈ Marginal |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n\n**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n\n**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n\nThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n\nReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n\nThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n\n⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n\n**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n\n**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n\n### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n\n| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n\nContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n\n### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n\n### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n\n**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n\n**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n\n**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n\n**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n| piqa | — | — | — |\n| winogrande | — | — | — |\n| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n\n**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------|---|\n| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n\n**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n\n## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n\nAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n\n| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n\n**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n\n**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n\n## Differentiation from RateQuant\n\n| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n|--------|-----------|------|\n| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 5/5 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n- **Statistical power**: n=5 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 5 architectures\" or \"5/5 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n","numLines":243,"startLine":1,"totalLines":243}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MpZHsFreGDESX2QDLrw9vZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me construct a complete LaTeX paper based on the \"worst\" tier narrative guidance:\n\nKey narrative reframing for worst tier:\n1. Cardinality constraint as universal safeguard (architecture-agnostic)\n2. Systematic negative result (non-uniform beneficial in only 1/6 cases)\n3. Compounding effect characterization (mechanism analysis)\n\nThe diagnostic/decision rule is downgraded since it has a false positive (Qwen14B). Title shifts to emphasize the cardinality constraint.\n\n\nI'm now compiling all ten experiments from the dataset into a comprehensive paper structure with corresponding tables and results sections for each. 4 Cross-Dataset Evaluation (Qwen7B)\n11. RateQuant Greedy Comparison\n12. Oracle Comparison\n13. Cross-Domain Calibration Robustness\n14. Head Sensitivity Visualization\n15. Downstream Task Evaluation\n16. 70B Profiling-Only\n17. K/V Separation\n18. L0-Only Heuristic Baseline\n19. RateQuant Greedy + Cardinality Constraint\n20. Multi-Seed Error Bars\n21. Runtime/Latency Benchmark\n22. W9 Compounding Scaling\n23. Qwen2.5-14B Downstream Eval\n\nLet me organize these into a coherent paper structure:\n\n- Abstract\n- Introduction\n- Related Work (brief)\n- Method\n  - Problem formulation (MCKP for KV cache)\n  - Cardinality constraint\n  - Profiling\n- Experiments\n  - Setup\n  - Cross-architecture profiling (covers exps 1, 5, 6, 16 - the profiling results)\n  - Cardinality constraint effectiveness (covers exps 2, 3, 7, 11, 19 - constraint results)\n  - Systematic negative result (covers exps 2, 5, 6, 15, 23 - the negative results)\n  - Compounding effect characterization (covers exps 7, 22 - compounding)\n  - Budget sweep (exp 8)\n  - Solver equivalence (exps 11, 12, 19)\n  - Ablations & robustness (exps 4, 9, 10, 13, 17, 18, 20, 21)\n- Analysis / Discussion\n- Conclusion\n\nNow I'm ready to write the full paper, pulling data from the experiments and structuring everything around the core narrative: constraints as a safeguard mechanism, the systematic negative result showing where the approach fails, and the compounding effect that emerges under certain conditions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30744,"cache_read_input_tokens":24075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30744},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60b94339-87f0-47ef-aa74-b7c45d2f68d8","uuid":"02c4d23d-36f7-42bf-a911-5af0ed4fc026"}
